:"The plan's tree listed `store.rs` for bindings and `fiber.rs` for `FiberData`; in the code, bindings and fiber data live in `state.rs` (provide / withdraw / get are in `service.rs`), and `context.rs`, `deps.rs` and `id_table.rs` are separate modules. The tree above follows the repository.","locale":"en"},"6123":{"id":"/en/docs/development-148","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#dependencies","content":"Crate dependencies mirror the TS packages: `core ← timer, logger-console, fs ← loader ← include, hmr ← kardia (facade)`; `hmr` also uses `fs` for its watch mode, and `kardia-guest` depends on none of them.","locale":"en"},"6124":{"id":"/en/docs/development-149","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#dependencies","content":"The diagram shows the direct dependencies in the `Cargo.toml` files. The chain above is a layering, not a list of direct dependencies: `kardia-loader` depends only on `kardia-core` (not on `timer`, `logger-console` or `fs`), while `kardia-include` and `kardia-hmr` each depend on `core`, `loader` and `fs`. The facade depends on every other crate except `kardia-guest`; `kardia-macros` depends on no kardia crate (its tests use `kardia-core`).","locale":"en"},"6125":{"id":"/en/docs/development-150","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#external-dependencies","content":"Kept deliberately small; each line says why it is needed.","locale":"en"},"6126":{"id":"/en/docs/development-151","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#external-dependencies","content":"Crate","locale":"en"},"6127":{"id":"/en/docs/development-152","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#external-dependencies","content":"Used by","locale":"en"},"6128":{"id":"/en/docs/development-153","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/