":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"**`create(options, parent, position)`** validates the options deeply (including a group's members) before anything is committed, assigns an id if there is none, inserts the entry at `position` (clamped; `None` appends) in the group of entry `parent` (`None` for the root group) and starts it. A group entry creates its group when its plugin loads, so a `parent` that is still loading is awaited. (Entries that come from a file or a group update are validated shallowly instead, each group member when its group reconciles it; `kardia_loader::validate_options(&options, deep)` is the check.)","locale":"en"},"7061":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"**`update(id, patch, parent, position)`** merges `patch` into the options (`null` deletes a key), validates the result and applies it. `parent: None` leaves the entry where it is; `Some(None)` moves it to the root group and `Some(Some(id))` into the group of entry `id`, also across trees: a move into another tree takes the entry's group members along and fails if one of their ids already exists there.","locale":"en"},"7062":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"What an update does to the running plugin depends on what changed:","locale":"en"},"7063":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"a changed `name` or `inject`, or an entry that is not running: the entry is rebuilt (its fibers disposed, then started again);","locale":"en"},"7064":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"otherwise the running fibers are patched in place: the entry is re-attached under its (new) group with its new isolation table (re-attaching an entry's context also moves every fiber below it, as with a re-pointed JavaScript prototype), `intercept` is swapped in place, and a changed `config` reaches the plugin as `fiber.update_with(config, true)`, which the plugin's update hook may take over instead of restarting.","locale":"en"},"7065":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"**`remove(id)`** disposes the entry and removes it from its group.","locale":"en"},"7066":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"**Write-back.** Changes a plugin makes to itself reach its entry:","locale":"en"},"7067":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"a plugin that disposes itself is persisted as `disabled: true`;","locale":"en"},"7068":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"a plugin that updates its own configuration (`fiber.update(..)`, which emits `ConfigCommitted`) has the new `config` written to its entry;","locale":"en"},"7069":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"a dependency loss unloads an entry's outer fiber without disposing it; the entry then reads as disabled until its outer fiber is reactivated, and nothing is written.","locale":"en"},"7070":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"Every change applied to a tree is reported to its backend as an `EntryChange`, after it has been applied:","locale":"en"},"7071":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"`EntryChange` fields","locale":"en"},"7072":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7073":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"`id`, `group`","locale":"en"},"7074":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"the entry's local id and the group it is now in","locale":"en"},"7075":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"`options` absent","locale":"en"},"7076":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"the entry was removed from `group`","locale":"en"},"7077":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"`legacy` absent","locale":"en"},"7078":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"the entry was created in `group`","locale":"en"},"7079":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"both present","locale":"en"},"7080":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"the entry was updated; `from` is the group it left if it moved within the tree","locale":"en"},"7081":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"A move into another tree is reported as a removal from the source tree and a creation in the target.","locale":"en"},"7082":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"A `TreeBackend` decides where a tree's changes go. Every method has a default:","locale":"en"},"7083":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`TreeBackend` method","locale":"en"},"7084":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"7085":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"7086":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`commit(&change)`","locale":"en"},"7087":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"nothing","locale":"en"},"7088":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"called synchronously after a change has been applied to the tree","locale":"en"},"7089":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`resolver()`","locale":"en"},"7090":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`None` (the loader's resolver)","locale":"en"},"7091":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"resolves plugin names for this tree","locale":"en"},"7092":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`handle()`","locale":"en"},"7093":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`None`","locale":"en"},"7094":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"the object behind the tree, for its owner to find it again","locale":"en"},"7095":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`locate(id, path, value)`","locale":"en"},"7096":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`None`","locale":"en"},"7097":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"where the value at `path` in the options of entry `id` is written; with `value`, only if that is the value written there; without, a missing value is located at its closest written ancestor","locale":"en"},"7098":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`locate_expr(id, path, expr, offset)`","locale":"en"},"7099":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`None`","locale":"en"},"7100":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"where char `offset` of the expression `expr` at `path` is written","locale":"en"},"7101":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"Entries set up isolation and interception declaratively.","locale":"en"},"7102":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"**`isolate`** gives the entry's services their own realm:","locale":"en"},"7103":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"`isolate: { db: true }` makes `db` private to the entry;","locale":"en"},"7104":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"`isolate: { db: shared }` puts `db` into a realm shared by every entry using the label `shared`.","locale":"en"},"7105":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"(The TypeScript loader names these realms `db#<id>` and `db@shared`; in kardia they are plain `RealmId`s, which print as `realm#<n>`.)","locale":"en"},"7106":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"When an entry's effective realms change (a new `isolate`, or a move to another group), a binding provided from inside the entry **migrates** to the new realm without restarting its provider, as long as the new realm is free; the consumers of both realms re-resolve. A shared realm is released once no entry uses its label for that service any more.","locale":"en"},"7107":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"**`intercept`** is metadata for the services the entry's plugin uses, keyed by service: `intercept: { logger: { name: db, level: 3 } }`. It is evaluated (it may contain expressions) and swapped in place, so a running plugin sees new metadata without a restart. A failing `intercept` disables the entry.","locale":"en"},"7108":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"**`inject`** as a map attaches metadata to a declared dependency: `inject: { loader: { await: true } }`. The metadata may contain expressions, evaluated in the parent group's context; a failure disables the entry.","locale":"en"},"7109":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"The `include` plugin (`kardia_include::IncludePlugin`) loads the entries of a YAML or JSON file as a subtree and keeps the file in sync both ways. It declares the `loader` service; with `watch` it also needs `fs`.","locale":"en"},"7110":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"7111":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7112":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"`path`","locale":"en"},"7113":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"the file, relative to the base directory of the tree the include entry is in (for a nested include, the directory of the including file); `.json`, `.yaml` or `.yml`","locale":"en"},"7114":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"`watch`","locale":"en"},"7115":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"re-read the file whenever it changes (needs the `std:fs` service)","locale":"en"},"7116":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"`initial`","locale":"en"},"7117":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"entries written to the file if it does not exist yet","locale":"en"},"7118":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"`patches`","locale":"en"},"7119":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"overrides and additions applied on top of the file (below)","locale":"en"},"7120":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"**Starting.** The include reads the file. If the file is missing and `initial` is set, it writes `initial` (with ids assigned) and reads that; without `initial` it fails with `config file not found: <path>`. Any other read, parse or validation failure fails the plugin, as does an unsupported extension (`extension \"toml\" not supported`). A file must be a top-level array of objects.","locale":"en"},"7121":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"**File edits → tree.** Each read is reconciled into the subtree; only the latest intended tree is applied, older ones are skipped. A file that fails to parse mid-edit (an empty or truncated file is routine while editing) is logged as a warning, the running tree stays as it was, and nothing is written until a later read succeeds.","locale":"en"},"7122":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"**Tree changes → file.** Runtime changes of the subtree (API edits, plugin self-updates and self-disposals) are recorded in a journal and written back to whoever owns them: the file, or a patch in the include's own configuration, which is persisted through the include's own entry in the parent tree. Shutting down does not write to the file.","locale":"en"},"7123":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"**Anonymous entries.** Entries the file leaves without an id get one before the loader sees them, and the id is written back. An anonymous entry that looks exactly like one from the previous read keeps that id (unless the file now names it explicitly), so editing a neighbour does not restart it.","locale":"en"},"7124":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"`patches` let a parent file adjust an included file without editing it:","locale":"en"},"7125":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"Patch","locale":"en"},"7126":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"7127":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"`{ insert: [..] }`","locale":"en"},"7128":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"appends entries to the included root","locale":"en"},"7129":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"`{ id, insert: [..] }`","locale":"en"},"7130":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"appends entries to the group `id`","locale":"en"},"7131":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"`{ id, name?, ..keys }`","locale":"en"},"7132":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"overrides keys of entry `id`","locale":"en"},"7133":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"A patch that does not apply (`patch insert: entry x not found`, `… is not a group`) is reported as a warning and owns nothing. Every inserted entry gets an id, so that runtime changes can be routed back to it. The include tracks who supplies each entry and key (the file, a patch overriding a key, or an entry written inside a patch), and writes a runtime change of a patch-owned value into the patch, not the file. New `patches` are applied in place when the include's configuration is updated; a different `path` or `watch` restarts it.","locale":"en"},"7134":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Atomic writes.** The include writes a temp file in the same directory (`.<name>.<pid>.<seq>.tmp`) and renames it over the file, so no reader sees a truncated file.","locale":"en"},"7135":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Stale-content check.** Before every rename, it checks that the file still holds the content it last read. If someone else wrote the file meanwhile, it reads and merges first, then writes again.","locale":"en"},"7136":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Transient failures.** A rename that fails with `PermissionDenied` or `ResourceBusy` (such as a virus scanner holding the file) is retried up to 10 times, waiting 20 ms longer each time.","locale":"en"},"7137":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Read-only or missing files.** Changes are kept in memory, with a warning: `config file <path> is read-only, N pending change(s) kept in memory` (or `is missing`). A failed write logs `failed to write config file <path>, N pending change(s) kept in memory`.","locale":"en"},"7138":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Conflicts: the file wins.** When the file changes while runtime changes are pending, the include merges three ways. Conflicting runtime changes are dropped so that the tree follows the file, and each drop is logged as `config conflict in <path>: entry <id> <reason>; file wins`, with one of these reasons:","locale":"en"},"7139":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`key \"k\" modified both in file and at runtime`","locale":"en"},"7140":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`removed in file, modified at runtime`","locale":"en"},"7141":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`modified in file, removed at runtime`","locale":"en"},"7142":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`added in file, removed at runtime`","locale":"en"},"7143":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`moved both in file and at runtime`","locale":"en"},"7144":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`Include::of(&tree)` returns the running include behind a tree it created:","locale":"en"},"7145":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7146":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"Does","locale":"en"},"7147":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.filename()`","locale":"en"},"7148":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"the absolute path of the file","locale":"en"},"7149":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.tree()`","locale":"en"},"7150":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"its `TreeHandle`","locale":"en"},"7151":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.refresh().await`","locale":"en"},"7152":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"re-reads the file and reconciles the tree with it (what a watcher triggers), then waits for every pending read and write","locale":"en"},"7153":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.flush().await`","locale":"en"},"7154":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"resolves once every pending read and write has been processed and the tree reflects the outcome","locale":"en"},"7155":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.stop().await`","locale":"en"},"7156":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-204","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"flushes what the user last did, then removes the tree's entries","locale":"en"},"7157":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-205","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`IncludePlugin::with_rename(rename)` is the plugin with a custom rename function in place of `std::fs::rename`, for fault-injection tests.","locale":"en"},"7158":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-206","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"In YAML, `!!js <source>` reads as an expression object `{ \"__jsExpr\": source }` and is written back the same way. Unknown tags are errors, since they would leave the data incomplete. Written YAML uses block style, with single-quoted strings where needed.","locale":"en"},"7159":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-207","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"Errors in config files point at the place they refer to, as `file:line:col`.","locale":"en"},"7160":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-208","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"**Read, parse and validation errors** of a file are a `ConfigFileError { stage, path, cause, issues }`:","locale":"en"},"7161":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-209","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"The first line names the stage (`read`, `parse` or `validate`) and, for a read failure, its cause; each issue follows with its position.","locale":"en"},"7162":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-210","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"**Entry errors** the loader logs (option and config validation, `ModuleNotFound`, expression failures) are located through the tree backend's `locate` / `locate_expr`. Each issue gets `(at <path>, file:line:col)`, an expression failure an `at <path> (file:line:col)` frame, and the entry and each ancestor that has a position an `at <id> (file:line:col)` frame:","locale":"en"},"7163":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-211","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"How values are located:","locale":"en"},"7164":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-212","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"the include locates a value where its owner writes it: in its file, or in a patch in its parent's file;","locale":"en"},"7165":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-213","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"a YAML alias is located at its anchor;","locale":"en"},"7166":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-214","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"a char of an expression is located through YAML escapes;","locale":"en"},"7167":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-215","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"a missing value is located at the key that should hold it (its closest written ancestor);","locale":"en"},"7168":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-216","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"a JSON file is located by parsing it as YAML as well (JSON is YAML), so it gets the same positions;","locale":"en"},"7169":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-217","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"values changed at runtime are not located, and an error that cannot be located at all is logged as it is.","locale":"en"},"7170":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-218","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"The loader does not expose an `Entry::evaluate` for evaluating expressions of an entry from outside.","locale":"en"},"7171":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-219","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"A custom `TreeBackend` gets the same output by implementing `locate` and `locate_expr`; `TreeHandle::locate` and `TreeHandle::locate_expr` call them for a local id.","locale":"en"},"7172":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-220","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"The loader patches an entry's context when the entry starts and when its options change in place: it re-attaches the context under its group, installs the isolation table and reconciles the running fibers. `loader.on_patch_context(ctx, hook)` wraps that step (the TypeScript `loader/patch-context` waterfall):","locale":"en"},"7173":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-221","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"The hook gets the entry and `next`, the rest of the chain as a future. `next` builds the rest only when it is awaited, so a hook runs after the ones registered before it, and a hook that does not await `next` stops the later hooks and the patch.","locale":"en"},"7174":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-222","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"Hooks run in registration order, inside the loader's own isolation step.","locale":"en"},"7175":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-223","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"The registration is an effect of `ctx`'s fiber, so the hook is removed with it.","locale":"en"},"7176":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-224","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"Unlike the TypeScript loader, the new isolation table is installed together with the re-parenting at the end of the chain, not before the hooks run.","locale":"en"},"7177":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-225","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"`EntryHandle::init().await` starts an entry if it is not running, or joins its pending start; concurrent callers share one start.","locale":"en"},"7178":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"page","content":"Writing plugins","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","locale":"en"},"7179":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","content":"Services and plugins in Rust: #[derive(Service)], #[plugin], the Plugin trait, PluginDef, and registering plugins for the loader.","locale":"en"},"7180":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#add-the-dependency","content":"Add the dependency","locale":"en"},"7181":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"A first example","locale":"en"},"7182":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services","content":"Services","locale":"en"},"7183":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"Providing a service","locale":"en"},"7184":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services-for-expressions","content":"Services for expressions","locale":"en"},"7185":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"Using a service","locale":"en"},"7186":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugins","content":"Plugins","locale":"en"},"7187":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-macro","content":"`#[plugin]` on an async function","locale":"en"},"7188":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-trait","content":"Implementing `Plugin`","locale":"en"},"7189":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#inject","content":"`Inject`","locale":"en"},"7190":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`PluginDef`: plugins from closures","locale":"en"},"7191":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#ctx-inject","content":"`ctx.inject`: an anonymous plugin","locale":"en"},"7192":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Starting plugins","locale":"en"},"7193":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The `Fiber` handle","locale":"en"},"7194":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"Configuration","locale":"en"},"7195":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"Stopping cleanly","locale":"en"},"7196":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"Loading your plugins from a config file","locale":"en"},"7197":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"Next","locale":"en"},"7198":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","content":"Plugins written in Rust are compiled into your app. This page shows how to declare services, write plugins that provide and use them, start them, and make them available to config files. Why the API looks this way is explained on API design.","locale":"en"},"7199":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#add-the-dependency","content":"`use kardia::prelude::*;` brings in the names most plugins need: `Context`, `Plugin`, `PluginDef`, `Inject`, `Injected`, `Service`, `Svc`, `Fiber`, `Result`, the two macros, the timer, `Loader`, `Deserialize` and `json!`.","locale":"en"},"7200":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"Services are plain types. The `#[plugin]` macro reads a plugin's dependencies from its signature, so accessing a service it did not declare is a compile error:","locale":"en"},"7201":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"What happens:","locale":"en"},"7202":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"`greeter` declares `database` and `timer`. It stays pending until both are available.","locale":"en"},"7203":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"`db` provides `database`, so `greeter` starts.","locale":"en"},"7204":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"Updating `db`'s config restarts it. `greeter` depends on it, so `greeter` stops first and starts again with the new database.","locale":"en"},"7205":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"Disposing `db` withdraws `database`: `greeter` stops, and its interval and the `closing` log line are reverted and run as part of the teardown.","locale":"en"},"7206":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"A longer, runnable version, which also hot-replaces the database implementation:","locale":"en"},"7207":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"With the facade crate `kardia`, both macros take `crate = ::kardia`. The generated code refers to `::kardia_core` by default, which only works if you depend on `kardia-core` directly.","locale":"en"},"7208":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services","content":"A service is any `Send + Sync + 'static` type bound to a **key**, a string. Keys are strings rather than type ids because config files name services.","locale":"en"},"7209":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services","content":"`#[derive(Service)]` uses the type name, hyphenated, as the key unless `name` is given. The `Service` trait has one more item, `merge_intercept`, which merges interception metadata; its default (a right-biased shallow merge of JSON objects) suits most services. See Services.","locale":"en"},"7210":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"A plugin provides a service from its `apply`:","locale":"en"},"7211":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7212":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"Provides","locale":"en"},"7213":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"`ctx.provide(value)`","locale":"en"},"7214":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"A `Service` value under its key","locale":"en"},"7215":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"`ctx.provide_arc(arc)`","locale":"en"},"7216":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"The same, from an existing `Arc`","locale":"en"},"7217":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"`ctx.provide_as(key, value)`","locale":"en"},"7218":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"Any value under an explicit key","locale":"en"},"7219":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"`ctx.provide_serialized_as(key, value)`","locale":"en"},"7220":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"A `serde::Serialize` value that also has a JSON view","locale":"en"},"7221":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"Providing is an effect of the providing plugin:","locale":"en"},"7222":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"The binding is withdrawn when the plugin stops. Its consumers stop first.","locale":"en"},"7223":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"One realm (a scope of services, see isolation) holds at most one binding per key. Providing a key that is already bound fails with `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided`, naming the provider.","locale":"en"},"7224":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"Consumers see the binding once the providing plugin is active.","locale":"en"},"7225":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services-for-expressions","content":"Expressions in config files and tooling read services as JSON. Only a service with a JSON view can be read this way: one provided with `provide_serialized_as`, or a `serde_json::Value` provided directly:","locale":"en"},"7226":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services-for-expressions","content":"An entry that injects `settings` can then use `disabled: !!js \"!settings.enabled\"`.","locale":"en"},"7227":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"Access","locale":"en"},"7228":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"Checked against","locale":"en"},"7229":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"Fails with","locale":"en"},"7230":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"`ctx.get::<S>()`","locale":"en"},"7231":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"The plugin's declared dependencies, at run time","locale":"en"},"7232":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"`AccessError::Undeclared` if `S` is not declared; `AccessError::Inactive` if it is declared but has no binding","locale":"en"},"7233":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"`Injected<D>::get::<S, _>()`","locale":"en"},"7234":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"`D`, at compile time","locale":"en"},"7235":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"A compile error if `S` is not in `D`","locale":"en"},"7236":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"`Injected<D>::deps()`, `ctx.deps::<D>()`","locale":"en"},"7237":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"All of `D` at once","locale":"en"},"7238":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"As `get`","locale":"en"},"7239":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"`ctx.get_as::<T>(key)`, `ctx.view(key)`","locale":"en"},"7240":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"A key given at run time (the JSON view for `view`)","locale":"en"},"7241":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"As `get`, or `AccessError::TypeMismatch`","locale":"en"},"7242":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"`ctx.live::<S>()`, `ctx.live_as::<T>(key)`","locale":"en"},"7243":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"Nothing: reads the current binding, if its provider is active","locale":"en"},"7244":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"Never fails; returns `Option`","locale":"en"},"7245":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"The checked accesses read the plugin's **committed view**: the bindings it resolved when it started. Access walks from the plugin's own provisions up through its ancestors, stops at an isolation boundary, and returns the first binding the plugin committed to. Because consumers read their committed view rather than the live store, a dependency stays readable while the consumer itself is being torn down (Theorem 70 in Metatheory). The root context has unchecked access to the live store.","locale":"en"},"7246":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"The typed accesses return `Svc<S>`, which dereferences to `S` and remembers the accessing context (the caller). Services such as `timer` use the caller to make what they do on your behalf an effect of *your* plugin; Services explains caller attribution, interception and events.","locale":"en"},"7247":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugins","content":"A plugin is the paper's component `(d, p, e)`: the services it depends on (`d`), the services it provides (`p`), and the effects it performs when it runs (`e`). There are four ways to write one.","locale":"en"},"7248":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-macro","content":"The function must be `async` and return `Result<()>`.","locale":"en"},"7249":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-macro","content":"The first parameter is `Context` (no declared dependencies) or `Injected<(A, B, …)>` (declares `A`, `B`, …; up to eight).","locale":"en"},"7250":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-macro","content":"The optional second parameter is the configuration, as `Arc<Config>`. Without it, the plugin takes no configuration (`()`).","locale":"en"},"7251":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-macro","content":"The macro generates a plugin type named after the function in CamelCase (`hello_world` → `HelloWorld`, `user` → `User`) and keeps the function.","locale":"en"},"7252":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-macro","content":"Arguments: `name` sets the plugin name (default: the hyphenated function name, `hello-world`), `provide` lists the keys it provides, `crate` the path to the kardia crate.","locale":"en"},"7253":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-macro","content":"With `Injected<D>`, `ctx.get::<S, _>()` compiles only if `S` is in `D` (the `_` is the inferred position of `S` in `D`). `Injected` dereferences to `Context`, so everything else on `Context` is available; `ctx.context()` gives the unchecked context.","locale":"en"},"7254":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-trait","content":"(`Key` is `kardia::Key`, `Arc` is `std::sync::Arc`.) The trait:","locale":"en"},"7255":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-trait","content":"`provide()` does not provide anything by itself: the plugin still calls `ctx.provide` in `apply`. The declaration lets kardia detect a dependency cycle when the plugin is started and log it as a warning, naming the plugins in the cycle (they stay pending), instead of leaving them pending silently.","locale":"en"},"7256":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#inject","content":"`Inject` is an ordered list of service keys, each with optional interception metadata:","locale":"en"},"7257":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#inject","content":"A plugin starts once every declared service is available, restarts when one is replaced, and stops when one goes away.","locale":"en"},"7258":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"A `PluginDef` is the type-erased form the runtime stores. You can build one from a closure:","locale":"en"},"7259":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"Constructor","locale":"en"},"7260":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"Configuration","locale":"en"},"7261":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"Registry identity","locale":"en"},"7262":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`PluginDef::of::<P>()`","locale":"en"},"7263":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`P::Config`","locale":"en"},"7264":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"The type `P`: every call gives the same identity","locale":"en"},"7265":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`PluginDef::typed(f)`","locale":"en"},"7266":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"Deserialized into the closure's `Arc<C>`","locale":"en"},"7267":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"New for every call","locale":"en"},"7268":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`PluginDef::new(f)`","locale":"en"},"7269":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"Raw `Value`","locale":"en"},"7270":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"New for every call","locale":"en"},"7271":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"and configure it with builder methods:","locale":"en"},"7272":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7273":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"Sets","locale":"en"},"7274":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`.name(name)`","locale":"en"},"7275":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"The plugin name, used in logs and by the logger","locale":"en"},"7276":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`.inject(inject)`","locale":"en"},"7277":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"Declared dependencies (anything that converts into `Inject`)","locale":"en"},"7278":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`.provides(keys)`","locale":"en"},"7279":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"Declared provisions","locale":"en"},"7280":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`.validate_with(f)`","locale":"en"},"7281":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"A check or transform of the raw configuration before it is decoded","locale":"en"},"7282":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`.tag(tag)`","locale":"en"},"7283":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"A marker that hosts such as the loader recognise","locale":"en"},"7284":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"The identity matters when replacing a plugin: `root.registry().replace(&old, &new)` swaps the implementation behind every running instance of `old`, keeping their place in the tree and their configuration. This is what hot reload does; `provider_consumer` shows it.","locale":"en"},"7285":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`Context::new()` creates a root context. Plugins started from a context become its children:","locale":"en"},"7286":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7287":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Takes","locale":"en"},"7288":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`ctx.plugin::<P>(config)`","locale":"en"},"7289":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"A typed configuration (`P::Config` must also be `Serialize`)","locale":"en"},"7290":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`ctx.plugin_value::<P>(value)`","locale":"en"},"7291":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"A JSON configuration","locale":"en"},"7292":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`ctx.plugin_def(&def, value)`","locale":"en"},"7293":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"A `PluginDef` and a JSON configuration","locale":"en"},"7294":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`ctx.inject(inject, f)`","locale":"en"},"7295":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Dependencies and a closure","locale":"en"},"7296":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Each returns a `Fiber`, the handle to that running instance. Starting a plugin is itself an effect of the calling plugin, so a child stops when its parent stops. Stopping the root (`root.fiber().dispose().await`) reverts everything.","locale":"en"},"7297":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The fiber handle offers:","locale":"en"},"7298":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7299":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Does","locale":"en"},"7300":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`state()`","locale":"en"},"7301":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`Pending` (waiting for dependencies), `Loading`, `Active`, `Unloading`, `Failed` or `Disposed`","locale":"en"},"7302":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`settled().await`","locale":"en"},"7303":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Waits until no transition is in flight; fails with the plugin's error","locale":"en"},"7304":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`update(value)?.await`","locale":"en"},"7305":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Replaces the configuration (below)","locale":"en"},"7306":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`update_with(value, no_save)`","locale":"en"},"7307":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The same; `no_save: true` skips the write-back to a config file","locale":"en"},"7308":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`restart().await`","locale":"en"},"7309":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Unloads and loads a non-failed plugin again; a failed plugin stays failed","locale":"en"},"7310":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`dispose().await`","locale":"en"},"7311":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Stops the plugin and removes it","locale":"en"},"7312":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`error()`","locale":"en"},"7313":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The error of the last failed load","locale":"en"},"7314":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`context()`, `config()`, `name()`, `parent()`, `effects()`","locale":"en"},"7315":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Introspection","locale":"en"},"7316":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"A `Failed` plugin clears its failure through `update` or an implementation replacement in the registry. Neither `restart()` nor a dependency refresh clears the error. `update_with(config, true)` can also recover it without emitting the `ConfigCommitted` event used for configuration write-back.","locale":"en"},"7317":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`Fiber::set_recovery` now selects `Manual` (default), bounded `Retry`, or `Host` handling. The supervisor outlives the failed instance, waits for cleanup and cancels on disposal or policy changes. Loader entries expose the same choice through `recovery`; see configuration and examples and native fault evidence. `restart()` still does not clear failure; manual handling uses `update`, while selected supervision drives the supported recovery operation. Unrelated plugins must remain operational under every policy.","locale":"en"},"7318":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"The configuration enters as JSON (from a config file, `plugin_value` or `update`) and is decoded once per load into `Config`, with serde:","locale":"en"},"7319":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"A decoding error names the failing path, such as `invalid config: … (at items.1)`.","locale":"en"},"7320":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"Unknown fields are tolerated, unless the config type opts into `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`.","locale":"en"},"7321":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"A missing configuration (`null`) is read as an empty object, so a config type whose fields all have defaults (`#[serde(default)]`) accepts it. `()` accepts anything.","locale":"en"},"7322":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"`fiber.update(value)` validates the new configuration first: a rejected configuration leaves the running instance untouched. The new configuration is then offered to the plugin's update hooks. If no hook takes it over, the plugin restarts.","locale":"en"},"7323":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"`ctx.on_update_with` does the same with a hook that returns the future `update` should wait for. A hook is an effect, so it goes away with the plugin.","locale":"en"},"7324":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"Everything a plugin registers through its context is an effect that is reverted when it stops: provided services, listeners, timers, child plugins, and plain disposers such as `ctx.on_dispose(…)`. Effects covers effects in full; two points matter while writing `apply`:","locale":"en"},"7325":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"**Register the inverse right after acquiring a resource**, so that nothing leaks if the plugin is stopped while starting.","locale":"en"},"7326":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"**`ctx.checkpoint()?`** is a point where a superseded load stops. It returns `Err(Interrupted)` when the plugin's target changed since the load began (it was updated, disposed or lost a dependency). Returning that error from `apply` is not a failure: the plugin unloads what it registered so far. kardia never cancels a running `apply` by itself.","locale":"en"},"7327":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"The loader resolves the `name` of each entry. To load your own plugins from a config file, register them in a `kardia::loader::Catalog` and pass it to `Loader::plugin`:","locale":"en"},"7328":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"`kardia::catalog()` holds every built-in plugin except `hmr` (which needs a module graph, see Hot reload), under its name and its TypeScript package name; `kardia::loader::builtins()` holds only `group`.","locale":"en"},"7329":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"An entry name that is not in the catalog fails with `ModuleNotFound`, located at the entry's `name`.","locale":"en"},"7330":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"`Loader::plugin` takes any `kardia::loader::Resolver`; `Catalog` is one. The `kardia` binary uses its own resolver that falls back to guest modules for names that are not built-in plugins: `crates/kardia/src/main.rs` shows the full setup, including `hmr`.","locale":"en"},"7331":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"Services\" href=\"/docs/guide-services\" description=\"Caller attribution, interception, events and the logger.\" />","locale":"en"},"7332":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"Effects\" href=\"/docs/guide-effects\" description=\"Effects, disposers, effect scopes and teardown.\" />","locale":"en"},"7333":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"Loader\" href=\"/docs/guide-loader\" description=\"Entries, groups, isolation and include from Rust.\" />","locale":"en"},"7334":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"API design\" href=\"/docs/development-design\" description=\"Why the plugin API looks the way it does.\" />","locale":"en"},"7335":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","type":"page","content":"HTTP and WebSocket services","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-server","locale":"en"},"7336":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server","content":"Use Server, ACL, Echo, Static and Proxy together, with configurable failure recovery.","locale":"en"},"7337":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"Run the complete example","locale":"en"},"7338":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-server#rust","content":"Register routes in a Rust plugin","locale":"en"},"7339":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-server#recovery","content":"Choose recovery behavior","locale":"en"},"7340":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server","content":"The Server family provides HTTP/1 and WebSocket routing, access control, echo, static files and reverse proxying. Each plugin owns its routes, connections, streams and tasks. Replacing a provider rebuilds its consumers while unrelated plugins keep running.","locale":"en"},"7341":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server","content":"These features are on the source main branch; this work did not publish a new crates.io release. Use source containing the Server acceptance commit. An older binary installed with `cargo install kardia` need not contain them.","locale":"en"},"7342":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"From the repository root:","locale":"en"},"7343":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"WebSocket clients can connect to `ws://127.0.0.1:5140/echo` or `/proxy/echo` and send text or binary messages. The example ACL accepts loopback Host values only. The CLI starts `fs` and `fs:local`. Static resolves relative paths against the working directory's file URL, so run this example from the repository root.","locale":"en"},"7344":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"The complete configuration runs all five packages. A minimal Echo configuration is:","locale":"en"},"7345":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"Plugin","locale":"en"},"7346":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"Configuration","locale":"en"},"7347":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"Dependencies","locale":"en"},"7348":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`server`","locale":"en"},"7349":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"Required `port`; host defaults to `127.0.0.1`","locale":"en"},"7350":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"None","locale":"en"},"7351":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`server:acl`","locale":"en"},"7352":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`allowedHosts: false` or a domain list","locale":"en"},"7353":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`server`","locale":"en"},"7354":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`server:echo`","locale":"en"},"7355":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"Mount with `intercept.server.path`","locale":"en"},"7356":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`server`","locale":"en"},"7357":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`server:static`","locale":"en"},"7358":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"Required `root`; index, exclude, errorPages","locale":"en"},"7359":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`server`, `fs`","locale":"en"},"7360":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`server:proxy`","locale":"en"},"7361":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"Required `target`; normally enable `http` too","locale":"en"},"7362":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`server`, `http`","locale":"en"},"7363":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`http`","locale":"en"},"7364":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"baseUrl, headers, timeout, rootCertificates","locale":"en"},"7365":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"None","locale":"en"},"7366":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`fs:local`","locale":"en"},"7367":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"Mounts the read-only `file:` provider","locale":"en"},"7368":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"`fs`","locale":"en"},"7369":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#example","content":"The catalog also accepts the actual upstream names: `@cordisjs/server`, `@cordisjs/server-acl`, `@cordisjs/server-echo`, `@cordisjs/server-static`, `@cordisjs/server-proxy`, `@cordisjs/http`, `@cordisjs/fs` and `@cordisjs/fs-node`.","locale":"en"},"7370":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#rust","content":"Declare `Inject::new().with(\"server\")`, then access the service through the plugin's own `Context` in `apply`:","locale":"en"},"7371":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#rust","content":"Return `Ok(None)` to use the supplied response, `Ok(Some(response))` to propagate a returned response, or `next.await` to continue. A request body can be consumed once. Response readers and the sending branch are separate, so inspecting a response does not consume its outgoing body. Use `Body::stream` to forward data without collecting it first.","locale":"en"},"7372":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#rust","content":"Dispose a returned `Route` / `WsRoute` to unregister it individually; plugin disposal also releases them. Pending HTTP callbacks and response sources are cancelled and awaited, and a WS route closes its connections. User callbacks and asynchronous cleanup run outside runtime locks.","locale":"en"},"7373":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#recovery","content":"The default is to remain failed until explicitly handled. Put `recovery` on the entry, beside the plugin's `config`:","locale":"en"},"7374":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#recovery","content":"Host mode requires an embedding host to register that name using `Loader::register_recovery_handler`. The standard CLI does not define the callback automatically; an unknown handler name is an error.","locale":"en"},"7375":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#recovery","content":"When embedding directly, configure the plugin's `Fiber`:","locale":"en"},"7376":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#recovery","content":"`Failure` says what failed: `phase` is `Phase::Start` when the constructor's `apply` returned an error or panicked, and `Phase::Running` when a running instance faulted. A start failure repeats identically on every retry, so a policy that wants to stop there returns `KeepFailed` for it. `attempts` is the automatic restarts this supervisor made before the failure.","locale":"en"},"7377":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#recovery","content":"A delay table waits each entry in turn, and its end is the limit; `window` starts the count over, so a plugin that faults once a day is not spent after its third fault forever:","locale":"en"},"7378":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#recovery","content":"The same table is configuration: `{\"mode\":\"delays\",\"delayMs\":[2000,10000,30000],\"windowMs\":600000}`. Every scheduled restart emits `RecoveryScheduled` with its `due_in` and `attempt`, so an interface shows a plugin that keeps failing before it stops.","locale":"en"},"7379":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#recovery","content":"Automatic supervision outlives the failed instance, waits for cleanup, and retries at a bounded rate. In manual mode, use `fiber.update(config)` to recover explicitly; `restart()` does not clear failure. Host handlers can keep the instance failed or return `RetryAfter`; handler errors and unwind panics are contained too. Disabling, removing, disposing or changing policy cancels the previous recovery action. Recovery does not write configuration back automatically.","locale":"en"},"7380":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-server-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-server#recovery","content":"Every policy must keep unrelated plugins operational. An ordinary request error stays local to that request; an instance failure withdraws its services and affects their consumers. Unwind containment cannot isolate a process-wide native crash: use the existing process or WASM guest boundary when required. See architecture and acceptance and the behavior reference.","locale":"en"},"7381":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"page","content":"Services, events and logging","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services","locale":"en"},"7382":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services","content":"Provide and consume services, attribute calls to their caller, isolate and intercept services, dispatch events and log.","locale":"en"},"7383":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Defining a service","locale":"en"},"7384":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Providing a service","locale":"en"},"7385":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Declaring dependencies","locale":"en"},"7386":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Accessing services","locale":"en"},"7387":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"Compile-time checked access","locale":"en"},"7388":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`Svc<T>` and the caller","locale":"en"},"7389":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Interception metadata","locale":"en"},"7390":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Isolation","locale":"en"},"7391":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"Events","locale":"en"},"7392":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"Listening","locale":"en"},"7393":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Dispatching","locale":"en"},"7394":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"Built-in events","locale":"en"},"7395":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"Hooks","locale":"en"},"7396":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"Logging","locale":"en"},"7397":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"Exporters","locale":"en"},"7398":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#example","content":"A complete example","locale":"en"},"7399":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services","content":"A **service** is a value that one plugin provides and other plugins depend on. The runtime tracks who provides what and who depends on what: a plugin that declares a service starts once the service is available, restarts when it is replaced, and stops when it goes away. This page shows how to define, provide and consume services, how calls are attributed to their caller, how isolation and interception change what a context sees, and how to use events and the logger.","locale":"en"},"7400":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services","content":"For the theory behind services see Reactive coeffects; for why the Rust API looks the way it does (string keys, `Svc<T>`, no `Proxy`) see API design; every place where kardia behaves differently from the TypeScript Cordis is listed on Status and deviations.","locale":"en"},"7401":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"A service is any `Send + Sync + 'static` type bound to a **key** through the `Service` trait:","locale":"en"},"7402":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Keys are strings because configuration files name services (`inject: [database]`). The runtime stores each value together with its type, so a key reached with the wrong Rust type fails with `AccessError::TypeMismatch` instead of being misread.","locale":"en"},"7403":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Usually you derive the trait:","locale":"en"},"7404":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Without `name`, the key is the type name hyphenated: `Database` → `database`, `FooBar` → `foo-bar`. `#[service(crate = …)]` points the generated code at `::kardia`; without it, it refers to `::kardia_core`.","locale":"en"},"7405":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"**Associated services.** Cordis's `foo.bar` associated services and `ctx.mixin` are JavaScript-object conveniences. In kardia a service named `foo.bar` is just another key. To \"extend\" another plugin's type, use an extension trait (compile time, see `Svc<T>` and the caller) or a registry service built on `kardia_core::IdTable` (run time). No accessor or mixin layer is ported.","locale":"en"},"7406":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Providing is an **effect** of the current fiber: it is reverted when the fiber unloads (see Revertible effects). Every method returns `Result<EffectHandle>`.","locale":"en"},"7407":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7408":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Provides","locale":"en"},"7409":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide(value)`","locale":"en"},"7410":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"a `Service` under `S::NAME`","locale":"en"},"7411":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_arc(arc)`","locale":"en"},"7412":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"an `Arc<S>` you already hold","locale":"en"},"7413":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_as(key, value)`","locale":"en"},"7414":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"any `Send + Sync` value under an explicit key","locale":"en"},"7415":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_arc_as(key, arc)`","locale":"en"},"7416":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"the same, from an `Arc`","locale":"en"},"7417":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_checked(key, arc, check)`","locale":"en"},"7418":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"a value whose availability also depends on a predicate `check`, evaluated per consumer with the consumer's interception metadata. The predicate runs under the runtime lock and must not call into the runtime.","locale":"en"},"7419":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_serialized_as(key, value)`","locale":"en"},"7420":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"a `Serialize` value that also has a **JSON view**, readable with `ctx.view(key)`, by loader expressions and by guest plugins. A `serde_json::Value` provided under a key (`provide_as`, `provide_arc_as`, `provide_checked`) is its own JSON view.","locale":"en"},"7421":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"What providing does:","locale":"en"},"7422":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**One binding per key and realm.** A second provider in the same realm fails with `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided`, whose message is `service \"database\" has been registered at <db>` (the name of the providing plugin).","locale":"en"},"7423":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**Notification follows the provider's state.** Consumers are notified at once only if the providing fiber is `Active`; otherwise they are notified when it becomes `Active`. When the provider leaves `Active`, its consumers are notified before any of its inverses run.","locale":"en"},"7424":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**Withdrawal waits for consumers.** Reverting the provision removes the binding and notifies the realm, then waits until every consumer that committed to this binding has finished its own cleanup, and only then removes the provision.","locale":"en"},"7425":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**A retired provider frees its realm at once.** Disposing a provider unbinds its live provisions immediately, so a successor can provide in the same realm while the old consumers still drain (they keep reading the old binding through their committed views).","locale":"en"},"7426":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**A stale load cannot provide.** A retired fiber whose load is still in flight may still register inverses (so nothing it acquired leaks), but its `provide` calls fail with `KardiaError::InactiveEffect`.","locale":"en"},"7427":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**Removal is postponed during a drain.** While a provider is unloading, its withdrawn provisions stay reachable to its descendants until the drain ends, so they can use inherited services during their own cleanup.","locale":"en"},"7428":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`.provides([..])` on a `PluginDef` (or `provide = [..]` in `#[plugin]`, or `Plugin::provide()`) only **declares** what a plugin provides. The declaration is metadata for tooling and for the dependency-cycle check; a plugin can provide undeclared keys, which simply escape the check.","locale":"en"},"7429":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"There is no in-place overwrite of a bound value. To change what consumers see, provide a new value (withdraw and re-provide, restart or update the provider), so that the change is observed.","locale":"en"},"7430":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"A plugin lists the services it needs in its **inject** declaration, an `Inject`: ordered keys, each with optional interception metadata.","locale":"en"},"7431":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Where the declaration goes:","locale":"en"},"7432":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Plugin form","locale":"en"},"7433":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Declaration","locale":"en"},"7434":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`impl Plugin for P`","locale":"en"},"7435":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`fn inject() -> Inject`","locale":"en"},"7436":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`#[plugin]` function","locale":"en"},"7437":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"the type of its context parameter, `Injected<(A, B)>`","locale":"en"},"7438":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`PluginDef::new` / `PluginDef::typed`","locale":"en"},"7439":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`.inject(..)`","locale":"en"},"7440":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"a closure plugin","locale":"en"},"7441":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`ctx.inject(deps, \\|ctx\\| async move { … })`","locale":"en"},"7442":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"a loader entry","locale":"en"},"7443":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"its `inject` field (see Configuration)","locale":"en"},"7444":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"The runtime keeps the fiber in step with its declaration:","locale":"en"},"7445":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"It stays `Pending` until every declared service is available, then loads.","locale":"en"},"7446":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"If a declared service is replaced by another binding, it unloads and loads again against the new one.","locale":"en"},"7447":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"If a declared service goes away, it unloads and waits in `Pending`.","locale":"en"},"7448":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"**Dependency cycles.** When a fiber is inserted, the runtime checks whether the declared `provide` and `inject` sets of the live fibers in its realm form a cycle through it. If they do, it logs a warning naming the cycle (`dependency cycle: a -> b -> a`) and the fiber stays `Pending`, instead of waiting silently.","locale":"en"},"7449":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7450":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Returns","locale":"en"},"7451":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Access","locale":"en"},"7452":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.get::<S>()`","locale":"en"},"7453":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<Svc<S>, AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"7454":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, through committed views","locale":"en"},"7455":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.get_as::<T>(key)`","locale":"en"},"7456":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<Svc<T>, AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"7457":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, by key, for any type","locale":"en"},"7458":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.view(key)`","locale":"en"},"7459":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<Value, AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"7460":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, the service's JSON view","locale":"en"},"7461":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.deps::<(A, B)>()`","locale":"en"},"7462":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<(Svc<A>, Svc<B>), AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"7463":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, a tuple of up to eight services","locale":"en"},"7464":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.live::<S>()`","locale":"en"},"7465":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Option<Svc<S>>`","locale":"en"},"7466":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"reflective: the live binding of the realm, if its provider is active; never fails for undeclared keys","locale":"en"},"7467":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.live_as::<T>(key)`","locale":"en"},"7468":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Option<Svc<T>>`","locale":"en"},"7469":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"the same, by key","locale":"en"},"7470":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"**Checked access** (the paper's Algorithm 6) resolves a key like this:","locale":"en"},"7471":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"A binding that a fiber on the way provides itself, in the same realm, is returned directly.","locale":"en"},"7472":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Otherwise the walk goes up through the fibers that derived the context.","locale":"en"},"7473":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"It stops at a context that isolates the key again (an isolation boundary): the key is undeclared.","locale":"en"},"7474":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"The first fiber that declares the key decides. It returns the binding that fiber **committed** to when it loaded; a fiber that declares the key but has no committed binding yields `Inactive`.","locale":"en"},"7475":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"The root context, which cannot declare `inject`, has **unchecked** access to the live store, as in Cordis.","locale":"en"},"7476":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Because checked access reads the committed view rather than the live store, a dependency stays readable while the consumer runs its own teardown, even if the provider is already gone from the store (Theorem 70 of the paper).","locale":"en"},"7477":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"The errors:","locale":"en"},"7478":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`AccessError`","locale":"en"},"7479":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Message","locale":"en"},"7480":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Undeclared { key }`","locale":"en"},"7481":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`cannot get property \"key\" without inject`","locale":"en"},"7482":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Inactive { key }`","locale":"en"},"7483":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`cannot get required service \"key\" in inactive context`","locale":"en"},"7484":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`TypeMismatch { key, expected }`","locale":"en"},"7485":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`service \"key\" is not of type …`","locale":"en"},"7486":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected<D>` wraps a plugin context whose typed accesses are checked against its declared dependencies `D` at compile time. The `#[plugin]` macro reads `D` from the signature and generates both the declaration and the wrapper:","locale":"en"},"7487":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected::get::<S, _>()`: the `_` is the inferred position of `S` in `D` (`kardia_core::index::I0` … `I7`); you never write it.","locale":"en"},"7488":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected::deps()` returns all of `D` as a tuple of `Svc`s.","locale":"en"},"7489":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected::context()` returns the underlying, unchecked `Context`, and `Injected<D>` dereferences to it, so every other `Context` method is available.","locale":"en"},"7490":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`#[plugin(name = \"…\", provide = [\"key\"], crate = path)]` takes an `async fn` whose first parameter is `Context` or `Injected<(..)>` and whose optional second parameter is `Arc<Config>`. It generates a plugin type named after the function in camel case (`greeter` → `Greeter`), with the hyphenated function name as plugin name unless `name` is given. Writing plugins is covered in Plugins.","locale":"en"},"7491":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Every access returns a `Svc<T>`: the service value together with the **caller**, the context that accessed it. Cordis attributes calls with a JavaScript `Proxy`; kardia makes the caller an explicit part of the handle.","locale":"en"},"7492":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7493":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Returns","locale":"en"},"7494":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`*svc` (`Deref`)","locale":"en"},"7495":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the service value","locale":"en"},"7496":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.caller()`","locale":"en"},"7497":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the accessing `Context`","locale":"en"},"7498":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.key()`","locale":"en"},"7499":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the key it was reached under","locale":"en"},"7500":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.impl_id()`","locale":"en"},"7501":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the identity of the binding (never reused, so a replacement by an equal value is observable)","locale":"en"},"7502":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.arc()`","locale":"en"},"7503":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the `Arc<T>`","locale":"en"},"7504":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.provider()`","locale":"en"},"7505":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the providing fiber (the service's definition site)","locale":"en"},"7506":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.logger()`","locale":"en"},"7507":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"a logger for work done on the caller's behalf: named by the caller's `logger` interception `name`, else after the providing plugin","locale":"en"},"7508":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.intercepts()`","locale":"en"},"7509":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the interception metadata of this access, outermost first","locale":"en"},"7510":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.meta()`","locale":"en"},"7511":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"that metadata merged with `S::merge_intercept`","locale":"en"},"7512":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"**Effects on the caller's behalf.** A service method that creates an effect for its caller registers it on `svc.caller()`. The effect then belongs to the caller's fiber and is reverted when the *caller* unloads, which is what Cordis's tracker achieves with `this.ctx`. Service crates expose such methods as **extension traits on `Svc<S>`**, which coherence allows because the trait is local. The timer service does this (simplified: the real `timeout` also reverts its effect once it has fired):","locale":"en"},"7513":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"So `timer.interval(..)` in `greeter` above stops when `greeter` unloads, not when the timer plugin does.","locale":"en"},"7514":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"**A service's own dependencies.** A service resolves its own dependencies through the `Context` it stored when it was constructed (its definition site), so no shadow contexts are needed. Two consequences differ from Cordis, where both follow the use site:","locale":"en"},"7515":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Interception metadata of the outer caller does not reach the services a service calls in turn; it stays on `Svc::caller()`.","locale":"en"},"7516":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Effects a service creates through its stored context belong to the service's fiber.","locale":"en"},"7517":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Interception attaches metadata to a key along a context chain, so that a service can behave differently per caller (paper Def. 26–27). The usual example is the logger: `logger: { name: db, level: 3 }` renames and re-levels the logger of everything below.","locale":"en"},"7518":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Where metadata comes from, outermost first:","locale":"en"},"7519":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"the metadata declared with the `inject` that admits the access (`Inject::with_meta`, or an entry's `inject: { key: meta }`);","locale":"en"},"7520":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"every `ctx.intercept(key, meta)` on the caller's derivation chain, outer to inner (a loader entry's `intercept` field adds one).","locale":"en"},"7521":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"`Svc::intercepts()` returns this list and `Svc::meta()` merges it with `S::merge_intercept`, by default `merge_shallow`: objects merged key by key, later values winning, like `Object.assign`. Override `merge_intercept` in your `Service` impl for another merge. On a context, `ctx.intercepts(key)` returns the chain's metadata and `ctx.intercept_meta::<T>(key)` merges and deserializes it (malformed metadata yields `T::default()`).","locale":"en"},"7522":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Metadata also reaches availability predicates: `provide_checked` hands the predicate the consumer's metadata. The loader uses this for `inject: { loader: { await: true } }`, which makes `loader` available to an entry only once every entry has settled.","locale":"en"},"7523":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Each key lives in a **realm**. By default all contexts share the key's root realm; isolating a key gives a context, and everything derived from it, a realm of its own:","locale":"en"},"7524":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7525":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Derives a context in which","locale":"en"},"7526":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.isolate(key)`","locale":"en"},"7527":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`key` lives in a fresh, private realm","locale":"en"},"7528":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.isolate_in(key, realm)`","locale":"en"},"7529":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`key` lives in a given realm (`RealmId::new()`), shared by every context isolated into it","locale":"en"},"7530":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.extend()`","locale":"en"},"7531":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"the context has its own mutable isolation and interception tables (an `Overlay`)","locale":"en"},"7532":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.extend_with(&overlay)`","locale":"en"},"7533":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"the context is backed by an existing `Overlay`, shared with other contexts","locale":"en"},"7534":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"A provider binds in the realm its context resolves the key to, and a consumer sees only the binding of its own realm. Checked access stops at a context that isolates the key again, so an isolated subtree cannot reach the outer binding through an outer declaration. Related queries: `ctx.realm(key)`, `ctx.has_isolation(key)`, `ctx.isolated_keys()`; and for tooling, `ctx.bindings(key)` and `ctx.binding_provider(key, realm)`.","locale":"en"},"7535":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"In configuration files, isolation is the entry field `isolate` (`{ db: true }` for a private realm, `{ db: shared }` for a realm shared under a label); see The loader.","locale":"en"},"7536":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"An event is a Rust type that implements `Event`. Listeners are registered per event type.","locale":"en"},"7537":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Output` is what each listener returns. `Bailable` decides whether a result stops a `bail` or `serial` dispatch, and whether it is a failure in `parallel`:","locale":"en"},"7538":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Output`","locale":"en"},"7539":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"Bails when","locale":"en"},"7540":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"Failure in `parallel`","locale":"en"},"7541":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`()`","locale":"en"},"7542":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"never","locale":"en"},"7543":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"never","locale":"en"},"7544":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`bool`","locale":"en"},"7545":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`true`","locale":"en"},"7546":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"never","locale":"en"},"7547":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Option<T>`","locale":"en"},"7548":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Some(..)`","locale":"en"},"7549":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"never","locale":"en"},"7550":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Result<T, Error>`","locale":"en"},"7551":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Err(..)`, or `Ok(v)` when `v` bails","locale":"en"},"7552":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Err(..)`","locale":"en"},"7553":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"Each registration is an effect of the current fiber, so a listener is removed when its plugin unloads. All return `Result<EffectHandle>`.","locale":"en"},"7554":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7555":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"Registers","locale":"en"},"7556":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.on(f)`","locale":"en"},"7557":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"a synchronous listener, after those registered so far","locale":"en"},"7558":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.on_prepend(f)`","locale":"en"},"7559":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"a synchronous listener, before those registered so far","locale":"en"},"7560":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.on_async(f)`","locale":"en"},"7561":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"an asynchronous listener (returns a future)","locale":"en"},"7562":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.once(f)`","locale":"en"},"7563":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"a listener that runs at most once, then removes itself","locale":"en"},"7564":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.listener_count::<E>()` counts the current listeners.","locale":"en"},"7565":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7566":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Behaviour","locale":"en"},"7567":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`ctx.emit(&event)`","locale":"en"},"7568":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"calls every listener; asynchronous ones are started, not awaited","locale":"en"},"7569":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`ctx.bail(&event)`","locale":"en"},"7570":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"calls synchronous listeners until one returns a bailing result, which it returns as `Some(..)`; asynchronous ones are started, not awaited","locale":"en"},"7571":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`ctx.serial(&event).await`","locale":"en"},"7572":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"calls listeners one after another, awaiting each, until one bails: `Ok(Some(..))` with its result, or `Ok(None)`","locale":"en"},"7573":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`ctx.parallel(&event).await`","locale":"en"},"7574":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"calls all listeners concurrently and collects failures and panics into an `AggregateError` (`one or more listeners of event E failed`)","locale":"en"},"7575":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Dispatch takes a snapshot of the listeners and skips those removed meanwhile. An event can restrict its audience with `filter`, which gets the context each listener was registered in.","locale":"en"},"7576":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"A listener that panics, synchronous or asynchronous, never takes the dispatching code down with it:","locale":"en"},"7577":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Mode","locale":"en"},"7578":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"A panicking listener","locale":"en"},"7579":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`emit`","locale":"en"},"7580":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"is logged (`panicked: <message>`); the rest still run","locale":"en"},"7581":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`bail`","locale":"en"},"7582":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"is logged and counts as not bailing; the rest still run. An asynchronous one, which `bail` only starts, is logged when it panics","locale":"en"},"7583":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`serial`","locale":"en"},"7584":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"stops the dispatch: `serial` returns `Err(..)` with the panic, and later listeners do not run","locale":"en"},"7585":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`parallel`","locale":"en"},"7586":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-204","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"is one of the failures in the `AggregateError`; the rest still run","locale":"en"},"7587":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-205","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"A listener's own `Err(..)` result is an answer, not a failure: it bails `bail` and `serial`, which return it as `Some(Err(..))`.","locale":"en"},"7588":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-206","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Unlike Cordis, `emit` does not let a failing listener abort the dispatch, and there is no generic `waterfall`: extension points that Cordis builds on waterfall events are typed hooks (below).","locale":"en"},"7589":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-207","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"The runtime emits these from the root, after each state change:","locale":"en"},"7590":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-208","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"Event","locale":"en"},"7591":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-209","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"Fields","locale":"en"},"7592":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-210","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"Emitted when","locale":"en"},"7593":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-211","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`PluginInserted`","locale":"en"},"7594":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-212","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`","locale":"en"},"7595":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-213","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber is created (`internal/plugin` on insertion)","locale":"en"},"7596":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-214","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`PluginRemoved`","locale":"en"},"7597":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-215","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`","locale":"en"},"7598":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-216","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber is retired (`internal/plugin` on removal)","locale":"en"},"7599":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-217","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`StatusChanged`","locale":"en"},"7600":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-218","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`, `old`, `new`","locale":"en"},"7601":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-219","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber changes state","locale":"en"},"7602":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-220","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`ServiceChanged`","locale":"en"},"7603":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-221","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`key`, `realm`","locale":"en"},"7604":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-222","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a binding of `key` in `realm` appears or disappears; delivered only to listeners whose context resolves `key` to that realm","locale":"en"},"7605":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-223","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`ConfigCommitted`","locale":"en"},"7606":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-224","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`, `config`","locale":"en"},"7607":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-225","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber's configuration is replaced through `update` (the loader's write-back point)","locale":"en"},"7608":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-226","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`Replaced`","locale":"en"},"7609":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-227","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`","locale":"en"},"7610":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-228","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber is moved to another plugin implementation by `registry.replace`","locale":"en"},"7611":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-229","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"Where Cordis uses waterfall events (`internal/config`, `internal/get`, `internal/update`), kardia has typed hooks. Each registration is an effect:","locale":"en"},"7612":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-230","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"Hook","locale":"en"},"7613":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-231","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"7614":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-232","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"`ctx.on_update::<C>(\\|config: &C\\| bool)`","locale":"en"},"7615":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-233","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"offers configuration updates of the current fiber to the hook before restarting it; returning `true` takes the update over (no restart). The hook sees the decoded configuration and is skipped if `C` is not the plugin's configuration type.","locale":"en"},"7616":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-234","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"`ctx.on_update_with::<C>(..)`","locale":"en"},"7617":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-235","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"the same; a hook that takes the update over returns the future that `update` resolves with","locale":"en"},"7618":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-236","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"`ctx.on_config(hook)`","locale":"en"},"7619":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-237","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"a configuration resolution hook (`ConfigHook`) for every fiber of the root: it gets the source configuration and the next stage, ultimately the plugin's own decoding. The loader uses it to evaluate expressions.","locale":"en"},"7620":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-238","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"See Revertible effects for how `update` uses these hooks, and The loader for the loader's own hook.","locale":"en"},"7621":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-239","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"The logger is part of the core. `ctx.logger()` returns a `Logger` bound to the current fiber:","locale":"en"},"7622":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-240","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"**Name:** the `name` of the context's `logger` interception metadata if there is one; otherwise the plugin name of the fiber (or of its nearest named ancestor, else `root`), hyphenated (`fooBar` → `foo-bar`, `snake_case` → `snake-case`).","locale":"en"},"7623":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-241","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"**Level:** the `level` of the `logger` interception metadata, if any. `logger.with_level(level)` sets it on a copy.","locale":"en"},"7624":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-242","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`ctx.logger_named(name)` creates a logger with an explicit name (still taking the level from interception). `svc.logger()` logs on a caller's behalf (see above).","locale":"en"},"7625":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-243","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"Level","locale":"en"},"7626":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-244","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"Value","locale":"en"},"7627":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-245","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`Level::Error`","locale":"en"},"7628":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-246","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`0`","locale":"en"},"7629":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-247","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`Level::Warn`","locale":"en"},"7630":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-248","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`1`","locale":"en"},"7631":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-249","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`Level::Info`","locale":"en"},"7632":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-250","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`2`","locale":"en"},"7633":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-251","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`Level::Debug`","locale":"en"},"7634":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-252","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`3`","locale":"en"},"7635":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-253","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"Messages take any `impl Display`; format with `format_args!`. Exporters therefore receive finished text: there are no `%`-directives or custom formatters as in Cordis.","locale":"en"},"7636":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-254","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"An `Exporter` receives every message:","locale":"en"},"7637":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-255","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"`ctx.add_exporter(Arc::new(exporter))` registers it as an effect of the current fiber. A message reaches an exporter if its level is at most `exporter.level(name)`, else the logger's level, else `Info`. A `Message` carries `sn` (a sequence number shared by all exporters receiving the same call), `ts` (milliseconds since the Unix epoch), `name`, `level`, `text` and the `fiber` that logged it.","locale":"en"},"7638":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-256","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"The root keeps a ring buffer of the most recent messages at or below the logger's level (1000 by default): `ctx.log_buffer()` returns them oldest first, and `ctx.set_log_buffer_size(n)` resizes it.","locale":"en"},"7639":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-257","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"The terminal exporter lives in `kardia-logger-console`: register `ConsoleExporter::new(ConsoleConfig { .. })` directly, or load the `logger-console` plugin from a config file (its options are listed in Configuration).","locale":"en"},"7640":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-258","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"There is no `tracing` bridge; the plan leaves a `tracing_subscriber::Layer` feeding exporters as an optional addition to `kardia-logger-console`.","locale":"en"},"7641":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-259","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#example","content":"A longer, runnable version also hot-replaces the database implementation:","locale":"en"},"7642":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"page","content":"TypeScript and Tauri","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","locale":"en"},"7643":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"The @kardiajs npm packages: the same plugin model in TypeScript, the bridge that connects a TypeScript runtime, such as a Tauri webview, to a Rust kardia app, and extension points for Vue interfaces.","locale":"en"},"7644":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"Two runtimes, one model","locale":"en"},"7645":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"The TypeScript runtime","locale":"en"},"7646":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"Failure isolation and recovery policy","locale":"en"},"7647":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#timer-failures","content":"Timer callback errors and cleanup","locale":"en"},"7648":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#bridge","content":"The bridge","locale":"en"},"7649":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#host","content":"Host: `kardia-bridge`","locale":"en"},"7650":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client","content":"Client: `@kardiajs/bridge` and `@kardiajs/tauri`","locale":"en"},"7651":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client-services","content":"Services from the client","locale":"en"},"7652":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"Vue interfaces","locale":"en"},"7653":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Where things belong","locale":"en"},"7654":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#protocol","content":"Protocol","locale":"en"},"7655":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"kardia composes a Rust app. When part of the app is TypeScript, as in a Tauri app whose interface runs in a webview, the `@kardiajs` packages give that side the same model: plugins, services, revertible effects and lifecycle. The **bridge** connects the two runtimes.","locale":"en"},"7656":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"Package","locale":"en"},"7657":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"Contents","locale":"en"},"7658":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/core`","locale":"en"},"7659":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"Contexts, fibers, revertible effects, reactive services, events and logging. No dependencies; runs in browsers and Node.","locale":"en"},"7660":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/timer`","locale":"en"},"7661":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`timeout`, `interval`, `sleep`, `throttle` and `debounce`, cancelled when their plugin stops","locale":"en"},"7662":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/bridge`","locale":"en"},"7663":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"The client side of the bridge","locale":"en"},"7664":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/tauri`","locale":"en"},"7665":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"The bridge's transport over one Tauri command and a `Channel`","locale":"en"},"7666":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/vue`","locale":"en"},"7667":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"Vue integration: contribution points, `<ExtensionSlot>`, composables, routes","locale":"en"},"7668":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`kardia-bridge` (crate)","locale":"en"},"7669":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"The host side of the bridge, in the Rust app","locale":"en"},"7670":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"Each runtime composes its own plugins. A Rust plugin cannot be a child of a TypeScript one or the reverse: an effect's inverse is a closure in one runtime's memory, and a service is a value there. So the bridge does not share a plugin tree. It keeps each side's view of the other in step:","locale":"en"},"7671":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"**Effects never cross.** Each side reverts its own.","locale":"en"},"7672":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"**Service availability crosses.** A service the host exposes appears on the client exactly while it is exposed, so a client plugin that injects it runs exactly then, and restarts when it is exposed anew.","locale":"en"},"7673":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"**Calls are asynchronous** in both directions. A call into the other side fails with `unavailable` when that side is gone, and with `timeout` when it does not answer.","locale":"en"},"7674":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"**Events** go from the host to every client, named.","locale":"en"},"7675":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"This is the arrangement the paper describes for crossing a process boundary (each process hosts its own context, and calls between them follow an asynchronous contract, see Related work).","locale":"en"},"7676":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"It is a port of Kardia's core rather than a wrapper of the TypeScript Cordis:","locale":"en"},"7677":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Plugins** are functions, classes or objects with `apply`, each with optional `name`, `inject`, `provide` and `Config` (any Standard Schema validator). `apply` may return a promise, or a function that runs when the plugin stops.","locale":"en"},"7678":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Services** are keyed by string. `ctx.get(key)` is checked access: it fails for a service the plugin did not declare. `ctx.live(key)` reads the live store without a check. A `Service` comes back as a view whose `caller` is the accessing context, Kardia's `Svc::caller`.","locale":"en"},"7679":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Effects:** `ctx.effect(scope => ...)` collects inverses with `scope.defer` or returns one. An asynchronous body is never cancelled: `scope.checkpoint()` ends it once the effect is disposed.","locale":"en"},"7680":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Lifecycle:** fibers move through `pending`, `loading`, `active`, `unloading`, `failed` and `disposed`, as in Rust. A plugin restarts when a dependency is replaced, waits when one leaves, and its provider keeps running until its consumers have cleaned up. `fiber.update(config)`, `restart()`, `ctx.onUpdate(...)` and `ctx.registry.replace(old, new)` (hot replacement, for Vite HMR) behave as in Rust.","locale":"en"},"7681":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Events** are named: `ctx.on`, `emit`, `bail`, `serial`, `parallel`. The runtime reports `internal/plugin-inserted`, `internal/plugin-removed`, `internal/status`, `internal/service`, `internal/commit` and `internal/replace`.","locale":"en"},"7682":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Isolation and interception:** `ctx.isolate(key, realm?)`, `ctx.intercept(key, meta)`, `ctx.interceptMeta(key)`.","locale":"en"},"7683":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"Where it differs from Kardia and Cordis is listed on Implementation status.","locale":"en"},"7684":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"These new APIs are included in npm version 0.2.0. Rust and JS supervise their own plugin instances. A Rust recovery setting does not configure a JS plugin's policy.","locale":"en"},"7685":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"`fiber.setRecovery(policy)` selects supervision for one plugin handle, surviving instance unload/reload. The default is `{ type: \"manual\" }`, with no forced restart. Only the failed instance and consumers of its unavailable services may be interrupted; unrelated plugins must continue working.","locale":"en"},"7686":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"Policy","locale":"en"},"7687":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"Behavior","locale":"en"},"7688":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"`{ type: \"manual\" }`","locale":"en"},"7689":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"Remains failed until the host calls `fiber.update(fiber.config, true)`, changes configuration or replaces the implementation","locale":"en"},"7690":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"`{ type: \"retry\", delay: 1000 }`","locale":"en"},"7691":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"Waits the specified milliseconds after cleanup, then recovers with current configuration; subsequent failures retry at the same interval","locale":"en"},"7692":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"`{ type: \"host\", handler }`","locale":"en"},"7693":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"Calls the host after cleanup; returns `{ type: \"keep-failed\" }` or `{ type: \"retry\", delay: 1000 }`, optionally through a Promise","locale":"en"},"7694":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"`fail()` starts failure handling synchronously; cleanup finishes asynchronously, and `settled()` rejects when the failure settles. Ordinary `restart()` does not clear failure; manual recovery uses `update`. Automatic recovery does not emit configuration write-back events. Retry delays must be finite, positive and at most 2,147,483,647 milliseconds, avoiding JS timer overflow and rapid retries. An unchanged `ValidationError` is not automatically retried, including when a host handler returns retry.","locale":"en"},"7695":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#recovery","content":"The host receives `{ fiber, error, signal }`. Policy changes, manual updates, implementation replacement and removal invalidate obsolete decisions; cancellation aborts `signal`. Pass it to asynchronous operations that support cancellation. The framework cannot terminate arbitrary Promises, but never schedules retries from cancelled decisions. A throwing or rejecting host handler is logged, leaving the plugin failed while unrelated plugins continue. The root context rejects `setRecovery` and `fail`; restarting the root is not a recovery mechanism for one plugin.","locale":"en"},"7696":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#timer-failures","content":"`@kardiajs/timer` catches synchronous throws and asynchronous rejections from timeout, interval, throttle and debounce callbacks, logging under the scheduling plugin. These are **operation errors**, not automatic instance failures; an interval may continue firing. Explicitly call `ctx.fiber.fail(error)` when an instance is no longer usable, so its selected policy handles recovery.","locale":"en"},"7697":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#timer-failures","content":"Disposal cancels future triggers, then waits for callbacks already in flight. A timeout's effect remains until its callback finishes. Managed callbacks therefore finish before the old instance's cleanup completes. Callbacks must return the Promise for their asynchronous work; detached tasks and native timers are outside this mechanism. Do not await disposal of the callback's own effect or owning fiber from inside that callback: it would wait for itself. Report an instance failure through the non-waiting `fail()` operation instead.","locale":"en"},"7698":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#timer-failures","content":"A shared JS thread cannot isolate infinite loops, runtime crashes or process termination, nor forcibly cancel an uncooperative Promise. These guarantees cover framework-managed errors and lifecycle operations; stronger isolation requires a separate execution boundary supplied by the application. Vue contribution error boundaries still isolate the contribution without stopping its owning plugin by default.","locale":"en"},"7699":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#host","content":"The app creates a `Bridge`, mounts its plugin, and routes client requests into `Bridge::handle`. Plugins inject `bridge` and expose services; an exposure is an effect of the exposing plugin, so it is withdrawn when that plugin stops:","locale":"en"},"7700":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#host","content":"`Bridge::handle` runs its work on the runtime the bridge plugin runs on, so a Tauri command can call it from Tauri's runtime. The Tauri glue is one command (the `kardia-bridge` crate docs show it in full):","locale":"en"},"7701":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#host","content":"Call `bridge.close_client(label)` when a window is destroyed. A reloaded page needs nothing: its new session replaces the old one with the same label.","locale":"en"},"7702":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client","content":"Host services appear as `host.<name>` and host events as `host/<name>` (the `prefix` option changes `host`).","locale":"en"},"7703":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client","content":"The client connects in the background and reconnects when the host's bridge restarts. Its plugin is active while disconnected; host services are simply absent. `bridge.status` and the `bridge/status` event report `connecting`, `connected`, `disconnected` or `replaced` (another webview with the same label took over; it does not reconnect).","locale":"en"},"7704":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client","content":"A failed call rejects with a `BridgeError` whose `type` is `unavailable`, `timeout`, `invalid` or `failed`.","locale":"en"},"7705":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client-services","content":"A client can provide a service to the host, as an effect of the calling plugin:","locale":"en"},"7706":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client-services","content":"The host sees it as a `RemoteService`, provided by the client's session fiber and withdrawn when the session ends:","locale":"en"},"7707":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client-services","content":"A client can close at any time, and the Rust app usually runs without any window open. So a host plugin should look a client service up when it needs it (`live_as`), rather than declare it in `inject`, which would stop that plugin whenever the window closes. The client provides its services again after every reconnect.","locale":"en"},"7708":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"`@kardiajs/vue` lets extensions contribute to a Vue interface: components, views, settings sections, commands, routes. A contribution is an effect of the plugin that makes it, so it leaves when that plugin stops, and the interface follows.","locale":"en"},"7709":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Contribution points** are `Contributions<T>` services (`defineContributions(key)` provides one). `register(item)` is an effect of the calling plugin; items are ordered by `order`, an `id` is unique, and `items` / `entries` are Vue-reactive.","locale":"en"},"7710":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**`<ExtensionSlot name>`** renders the components of a point, in order. Each one gets the context of the plugin that contributed it, so inside it `useContext()`, `usePlugin()` and `useService()` act as that plugin, and its effects stop with it. `props` go to every component, under each contribution's own; the default slot shows while there is nothing; the `item` slot (`{ item, owner }`) renders each contribution itself.","locale":"en"},"7711":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Failing contributions** are contained: a contribution that throws (in setup, render, a hook, a watcher or a handler) is replaced by the `error` slot (`{ error, item, owner, retry }`), or by nothing without one, while the other contributions keep rendering and the error does not reach the app. `retry()` mounts it again. `@error` (`{ error, item, owner }`) reports the failure, for example to show which plugin failed; without it, the failure is logged by the owner's logger. The owner's plugin keeps running: a broken view is one contribution of the plugin, and stopping the plugin would also remove its services and its other contributions. To stop it, call `owner.fiber.dispose()` from `@error`.","locale":"en"},"7712":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Composables:** `useContext()`; `usePlugin(plugin, config)` runs a plugin for the lifetime of a component; `useService(key)` is a ref that follows a service (`undefined` while none is provided); `useContributions(key)` is a computed list for custom rendering, such as a navigation menu; `useFiberState(fiber)` follows a fiber.","locale":"en"},"7713":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Routes:** `addRoute(ctx, router, route)` adds a vue-router route as an effect: it is removed when the plugin stops.","locale":"en"},"7714":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Rust-only extensions** cannot ship Vue code, but a Rust plugin can expose a value describing its UI (a settings schema, say) and a TypeScript plugin can register a generic component for it.","locale":"en"},"7715":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"Third-party UI code runs with the webview's full access to Tauri: load only trusted code into the main webview, and give untrusted extensions declarative contributions or a sandboxed webview.","locale":"en"},"7716":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Belongs to","locale":"en"},"7717":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Backend capabilities, state, settings, persistence","locale":"en"},"7718":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Rust plugins on kardia","locale":"en"},"7719":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Interface composition: settings sections, commands, renderers, panels","locale":"en"},"7720":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"TypeScript plugins on `@kardiajs/core`","locale":"en"},"7721":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Which host services a client can see, and calls into them","locale":"en"},"7722":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"the host's `expose`, through the bridge","locale":"en"},"7723":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Transport, window identity, permissions","locale":"en"},"7724":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Tauri (one command, one `Channel` per session, capabilities)","locale":"en"},"7725":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"An extension can be Rust only (most backend capabilities; the interface renders what it exposes), TypeScript only (a panel or command using existing host services), or both: a Rust plugin that exposes a service, and a TypeScript plugin that injects `host.<name>`, so the interface half runs exactly while the backend half does.","locale":"en"},"7726":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#protocol","content":"The protocol (version 1) is JSON, tagged by `type`, with camelCase fields; unknown fields are ignored. The `kardia-bridge` crate docs list every request and message. Any transport works: the bridge's end-to-end tests drive the Rust host over stdin and stdout (`crates/kardia-bridge/examples/stdio_host.rs`).","locale":"en"},"7727":{"id":"/en/docs/guide","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","type":"page","content":"Guide","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide","locale":"en"},"7728":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"How to use kardia: config files, plugins, services, effects, the loader, hot reload and guest plugins.","locale":"en"},"7729":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide#which-page-do-i-need","content":"Which page do I need?","locale":"en"},"7730":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"The guide explains how to build apps with kardia, from the config file of the `kardia` binary to plugins written in Rust and guest plugins that reload in place. It assumes kardia is installed; Quick start shows a running app first.","locale":"en"},"7731":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"<Card title=\"The configuration file\" href=\"/docs/guide-configuration\" description=\"Entries and their fields, expressions, two-way sync, and the built-in plugins.\" />","locale":"en"},"7732":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"<Card title=\"Writing plugins\" href=\"/docs/guide-plugins\" description=\"Services and plugins in Rust: #[derive(Service)], #[plugin], PluginDef, and registering plugins for the loader.\" />","locale":"en"},"7733":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"<Card title=\"Services\" href=\"/docs/guide-services\" description=\"Providing and using services, caller attribution, interception, events and the logger.\" />","locale":"en"},"7734":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"<Card title=\"Effects\" href=\"/docs/guide-effects\" description=\"Revertible effects, disposers, effect scopes and how a plugin is torn down.\" />","locale":"en"},"7735":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"tex