ontent":"The Cordis commit kardia tracks is `6ad12cf2` (2026-11-27). It is not a floating `main`: `UPSTREAM_SHA` in `js/tests/server-parity/upstream.ts` is the one place that records it, and `bun run test:server-reference` checks the `cordis/` checkout is at that HEAD before running, failing when it is not.","locale":"en"},"7770":{"id":"/en/docs-23","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#baseline","content":"The Server contracts hold against the five packages at that commit (core, ACL, Echo, Static and Proxy, all `2.0.0-rc.0`). The Cordis reference section has an older fixed point of its own for the historical analysis of the core code; the two do not affect each other, as that page explains.","locale":"en"},"7771":{"id":"/en/docs-24","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#baseline","content":"Following a newer upstream commit means changing `UPSTREAM_SHA`, and the commit and package versions the pages cite.","locale":"en"},"7772":{"id":"/en/docs-25","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"Besides the user documentation (Getting started and the Guide), the documentation has three layers. Each one is a section of this site:","locale":"en"},"7773":{"id":"/en/docs-26","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"Layer","locale":"en"},"7774":{"id":"/en/docs-27","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"What it describes","locale":"en"},"7775":{"id":"/en/docs-28","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"Section","locale":"en"},"7776":{"id":"/en/docs-29","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"**Theory**","locale":"en"},"7777":{"id":"/en/docs-30","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"