e":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`interval(cb, ms) → dispose`","locale":"en"},"7917":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"effect around `setInterval`","locale":"en"},"7918":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`interval(ms) → AsyncIterableIterator`","locale":"en"},"7919":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"each tick resolves only the oldest pending `next()`; ticks without a waiter are dropped; `return()`/`throw()` semantics of async iterators; fiber disposal rejects pending reads","locale":"en"},"7920":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`throttle(cb, ms, noTrailing?)`","locale":"en"},"7921":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"leading call, trailing call with latest args unless `noTrailing`; `.dispose()`","locale":"en"},"7922":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`debounce(cb, ms)`","locale":"en"},"7923":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"each call restarts the timer; `.dispose()`","locale":"en"},"7924":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"`shared.ts`, `index.ts`, `browser.ts`. A class plugin (`name = 'logger-console'`) whose constructor calls `ctx.logger.exporter(this)`, so the exporter lives exactly as long as the plugin (see Logger).","locale":"en"},"7925":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"Config: `colors` (Node default from `supports-color`), `maxLength`, per-name `levels`, `showDiff`, a `showTime` template, `label { width, margin, align }`.","locale":"en"},"7926":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"It renders a `[E]/[W]/[I]/[D]` prefix, a hashed-colour label, aligned continuation lines and an optional `+Nms` diff; `%o` uses `util.inspect`.","locale":"en"},"7927":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"The browser build delegates to `console.*`.","locale":"en"},"7928":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"The following describes the historical watcher baseline. Current Rust `fs` additionally supports baseUrl, URL resolution, provider mounts and cancellable read streams, with explicit `fs:local` file reads. See Server auxiliary services for the newer fixed upstream scope.","locale":"en"},"7929":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"`index.ts`, `watcher.ts`. Service `fs`, currently only `watch(path, { filter }) → Watcher`.","locale":"en"},"7930":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"Paths resolve relative to the **caller's** `ctx.baseUrl`; `file:` URLs are accepted; Windows drive-relative forms are rejected.","locale":"en"},"7931":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"A single file is watched **through its parent directory** (`depth: 0`), so atomic rename-based writes do not lose the watch.","locale":"en"},"7932":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"The `Watcher` is an async effect wrapping chokidar (`ignoreInitial`), registered after the initial scan. Only `change` events are forwarded; `ready` replays asynchronously to late listeners; dispatch uses a snapshot; listener errors go to `error` listeners (whose own errors are only logged).","locale":"en"},"7933":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"The filter consists of gitignore-like rules: **last match wins**, tested against the entry *or any ancestor*. A directory is still traversed if a later including rule's literal base is related; patterns leaving the root are rejected.","locale":"en"},"7934":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"`index.ts`, `agent.ts`, `manifest.ts`, `backup.ts`, `process.ts`, `state.ts`. Service `packageManager`: transactional dependency installs driving npm / pnpm / yarn classic / yarn berry (hoisted `node_modules` only).","locale":"en"},"7935":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"`install(changes, { signal })` is serialized:","locale":"en"},"7936":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Detect the agent from `package.json#packageManager` (exact version, verified by `--version`), require a lockfile, and check the layout.","locale":"en"},"7937":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Snapshot the install state and back up the manifest, lockfiles and rc files (mode- and symlink-preserving).","locale":"en"},"7938":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Edit `package.json` (preserving indentation, EOL and sort order).","locale":"en"},"7939":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Run the agent with an **inactivity timeout** and abort support.","locale":"en"},"7940":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Diff the install state (`added/removed/updated`, with real paths).","locale":"en"},"7941":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"On failure: restore the files and run a **non-cancellable recovery install**; if that fails too, throw an `AggregateError`.","locale":"en"},"7942":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Processes are spawned in their own process group (POSIX) and the whole tree is killed (SIGTERM → SIGKILL; `taskkill /T` on Windows). The environment is scrubbed of variables leaked by an outer `yarn run`.","locale":"en"},"7943":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Real paths use Node's JS `realpath` algorithm so that they match module URLs (intended to feed hmr roots; not wired up in the repository).","locale":"en"},"7944":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#loader-utils","content":"`index.ts`, `internal.ts`. `unwrapExports` (ESM/esbuild interop) and `ModuleLoader.fromInternal()`, which gives access to Node's internal cascaded ESM loader (its shape is detected by API presence across Node 22–24.12+). Pure Node glue; **no Rust counterpart**.","locale":"en"},"7945":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"`create/src/index.ts`, `bin.ts`. A standalone scaffolding CLI (it does not use core):","locale":"en"},"7946":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"prompt for a name and prepare the directory;","locale":"en"},"7947":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"fetch the template package (`@cordisjs/boilerplate`) tarball from the configured npm registry and extract it with `strip: 1`;","locale":"en"},"7948":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"optionally stage a pinned Yarn binary (five documented rules);","locale":"en"},"7949":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"rewrite `package.json`, optionally `git init`, install and start.","locale":"en"},"7950":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"Errors print a fixed message and `process.exit(1)` (the tests run it as a child process). The `--mirror` flag is parsed but unused.","locale":"en"},"7951":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#port","content":"timer, fs and the logger exporters are thin wrappers proving that **\"lifetime by effect\" + caller attribution** is enough to make arbitrary resources revertible: exactly the paper's §6.1 acquisition-inside-the-boundary pattern (see Discussion and related work).","locale":"en"},"7952":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#port","content":"package-manager and create are Node-ecosystem tools; for a Rust framework they are optional or must be retargeted (e.g. Cargo / WASM component packages).","locale":"en"},"7953":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"page","content":"Context and reflection","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context","locale":"en"},"7954":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context","content":"How Cordis core represents contexts, stores service bindings per realm, notifies dependents and resolves coeffects through a Proxy.","locale":"en"},"7955":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#context","content":"`Context`: the first-class context","locale":"en"},"7956":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"Construction","locale":"en"},"7957":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"Derivation with `extend()`","locale":"en"},"7958":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#realm-symbols","content":"Realm symbols","locale":"en"},"7959":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`ReflectService`","locale":"en"},"7960":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#impl","content":"`Impl`: a binding","locale":"en"},"7961":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"`provide(name, value?, check?)`: coeffect provision","locale":"en"},"7962":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#set","content":"`set(name, value)`","locale":"en"},"7963":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#get","content":"`get(name, strict = true)` and `_getImpl`","locale":"en"},"7964":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#notify","content":"`notify(names, filter?)`: reactive notification","locale":"en"},"7965":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`accessor` and `mixin`","locale":"en"},"7966":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"Property access through the Proxy","locale":"en"},"7967":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"`locate(ctx, name)`: the committed-view walk","locale":"en"},"7968":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"Interception","locale":"en"},"7969":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"Design observations","locale":"en"},"7970":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/context.ts`, `reflect.ts` and `utils.ts`. The paper counterparts are §3.2 (coeffects, see Reactive coeffects), §5.1.2 (Algorithms 2–3) and §5.1.4 (Algorithm 6), both in Implementation.","locale":"en"},"7971":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#context","content":"`context.ts` declares:","locale":"en"},"7972":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"`new Context()` builds the **root** (`context.ts:36-49`):","locale":"en"},"7973":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It creates empty `isolate`/`intercept` tables (`Object.create(null)`).","locale":"en"},"7974":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It wraps itself in a `Proxy` with `ReflectService.handler`. This proxy *is* the context everybody sees; `this[symbols.root] = self`.","locale":"en"},"7975":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It creates the **root fiber** `new Fiber(self, {}, {}, null, …)` (runtime `null` ⇒ root, uid 0, `ACTIVE`).","locale":"en"},"7976":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It instantiates the four built-in services on the root: `reflect`, `registry`, `events`, `logger`.","locale":"en"},"7977":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It calls `this.fiber._disposables.clear()`. The built-in mixins and accessors registered during construction are *not* part of the root fiber's revertible effects: they must survive `root.fiber.dispose()`.","locale":"en"},"7978":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"`context.ts:55-63`:","locale":"en"},"7979":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"Every derived context is a **prototype-chain child** of its parent. This realizes the paper's *derived realization* (Definition 23): the child overrides some slots and inherits everything else. Nothing needs to be undone; dropping the child object discards the adjustment.","locale":"en"},"7980":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"`isolate(name, label?)` (`context.ts:65`) creates `Object.create(this[symbols.isolate])`, sets `shadow[name] = label ?? Symbol(name)` and extends with it. A fresh symbol gives a private realm; a shared `label` gives a shared realm.","locale":"en"},"7981":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"`intercept(name, config)` (`context.ts:73`) follows the same pattern for the intercept table.","locale":"en"},"7982":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"A fiber's context is `parent.extend({ fiber: this })` (`fiber.ts:150`).","locale":"en"},"7983":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"**Key property:** the isolation and interception tables are *prototype chains*. A lookup (`table[name]`) sees the nearest override; `Object.hasOwn(table, name)` detects an isolation boundary introduced at exactly that level (used by `locate`).","locale":"en"},"7984":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#realm-symbols","content":"`ReflectService.provide` lazily assigns a root realm: `ctx[symbols.root][symbols.isolate][name] ??= Symbol(name)` (`reflect.ts:222`). Thus *every* service name has a realm symbol in the root table once it has been provided; isolated contexts override it. The **store is keyed by realm symbol**, which gives the two-layer `k → ρ(k) → σ(ρ(k))` resolution of Definition 24.","locale":"en"},"7985":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`reflect.ts` holds the shared, root-level tables:","locale":"en"},"7986":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"7987":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"Paper","locale":"en"},"7988":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7989":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`store: Dict<Impl, symbol>`","locale":"en"},"7990":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"σ (`@@store`)","locale":"en"},"7991":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"realm symbol → current `Impl` (binding)","locale":"en"},"7992":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`props: Dict<Property>`","locale":"en"},"7993":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"–","locale":"en"},"7994":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"declared context properties: `{type:'service'}` or `{type:'accessor', get, set}`","locale":"en"},"7995":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`_implCounter`","locale":"en"},"7996":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"fresh names","locale":"en"},"7997":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"uid source for `Impl`s (never reused)","locale":"en"},"7998":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#impl","content":"`reflect.ts:65-75`:","locale":"en"},"7999":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"`reflect.ts:213-249`. `provide` is a `fiber.effect` (therefore tracked and revertible) whose callback:","locale":"en"},"8000":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"registers or validates `props[name]` as a service (an error if it is already an accessor);","locale":"en"},"8001":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"ensures a root realm symbol and computes `key = ctx[isolate][name]`;","locale":"en"},"8002":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"performs the **single-source check**: it throws `service \"x\" has been registered at <fiber>` if `store[key]` exists (O-Insert's disjointness, per realm);","locale":"en"},"8003":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"sets `store[key] = impl` and `fiber.provisions.add(impl)`;","locale":"en"},"8004":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"if the providing fiber is already `ACTIVE`, calls `notify([name])` immediately; otherwise notification happens when the fiber becomes `ACTIVE` (`Fiber._updateState`), matching \"only Active fibers provide\".","locale":"en"},"8005":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"Its **inverse** is async:","locale":"en"},"8006":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"delete the store entry (if it still holds this impl) and `notify` dependents in the impl's realm;","locale":"en"},"8007":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"the **provider-side guard**: `await` until `impl.dependents` is empty (`impl.release` is resolved by the last dependent's unload). It always yields at least once, so child cleanup can still access the inherited service;","locale":"en"},"8008":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"remove the impl from `fiber.provisions`.","locale":"en"},"8009":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#set","content":"`reflect.ts:200-211`. An in-place overwrite of the *own* binding (`impl.value = value`); an error if the name is not provided or is provided by another fiber. There is **no notification**: as the paper notes, an in-place overwrite is not observed by dependents.","locale":"en"},"8010":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#get","content":"`reflect.ts:188-198`. Resolves `ctx[isolate][name]` → `store[key]`. In `strict` mode it returns nothing unless `impl.ctx.fiber.state === ACTIVE` (**provider availability = Active**). It never throws.","locale":"en"},"8011":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#notify","content":"`reflect.ts:251-270`:","locale":"en"},"8012":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#notify","content":"This is Algorithm 3. The *filter* parameter exists so that the loader can replace the realm test during realm reassignment (Algorithm 7, see Managed realms).","locale":"en"},"8013":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`accessor(name, {get, set})` and `mixin(source, keys)` live at `reflect.ts:272-308`.","locale":"en"},"8014":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`accessor` declares a computed context property (as a revertible effect).","locale":"en"},"8015":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`mixin('events', ['on', 'emit', …])` exposes members of a service as context properties (`ctx.on` → `ctx.events.on`) bound to the accessing context. It is a generator effect that yields one accessor per key.","locale":"en"},"8016":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"The root wires (`reflect.ts:182-185`):","locale":"en"},"8017":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"8018":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"Keys mixed into the context","locale":"en"},"8019":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`reflect`","locale":"en"},"8020":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`get`, `set`, `provide`, `accessor`, `mixin`","locale":"en"},"8021":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`fiber`","locale":"en"},"8022":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`runtime`, `effect`","locale":"en"},"8023":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`registry`","locale":"en"},"8024":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`inject`, `plugin`","locale":"en"},"8025":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`events`","locale":"en"},"8026":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`on`, `once`, `parallel`, `emit`, `serial`, `bail`, `waterfall`","locale":"en"},"8027":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"`ReflectService.handler` (`reflect.ts:105-170`) mediates `ctx.foo` in its `get` trap:","locale":"en"},"8028":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"*special* properties (symbols, `prototype`, `then`, numeric strings, names starting with `_`) bypass mediation;","locale":"en"},"8029":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-75","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"ordinary own or inherited properties are returned through `getTraceable` (see Services and traceability);","locale":"en"},"8030":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-76","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"a declared **accessor** → its getter;","locale":"en"},"8031":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-77","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"if the *def site* (the shadow, see Services and traceability) is the **root fiber** → unchecked `reflect.get(prop, false)` (root code cannot declare `inject`);","locale":"en"},"8032":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-78","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"otherwise a `waterfall('internal/get', …)` (which lets plugins hook access) around `locate(defSite, prop)`:","locale":"en"},"8033":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-79","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"impl found → its value (traced);","locale":"en"},"8034":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-80","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"the fiber declares the key but has no committed impl → `cannot get required service \"x\" in inactive context`;","locale":"en"},"8035":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-81","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"nobody declares it → `cannot get property \"x\" without inject`.","locale":"en"},"8036":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-82","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"The `set` trap: an undeclared property on a non-root fiber → the error `cannot set property without provide`; an accessor → its setter; a service → `waterfall('internal/set')` → `reflect.set`.","locale":"en"},"8037":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-83","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"Errors are created as cheap placeholders and only materialized with a trimmed stack when thrown (`createAccessError`/`enhanceAccessError`).","locale":"en"},"8038":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-84","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"`reflect.ts:83-102` implements Algorithm 6, extended with own provisions and isolation boundaries:","locale":"en"},"8039":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-85","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"Consequences, all covered by `tests/isolate.spec.ts` and `reflect.spec.ts`:","locale":"en"},"8040":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-86","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"a consumer reads the **committed** impl, not the live store, so it keeps seeing its dependency during its own teardown (Theorem 70);","locale":"en"},"8041":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-87","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"a child plugin *inherits* the injection of an ancestor (`inject` declared on an ancestor admits access in descendants);","locale":"en"},"8042":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-88","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"an isolation boundary stops inheritance (`does not inherit the injected view across isolation boundaries`).","locale":"en"},"8043":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-89","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"`Service[symbols.resolveIntercept]` (`service.ts:57-70`) resolves the metadata for a service named `name` at access time:","locale":"en"},"8044":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-90","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"walk the context's intercept prototype chain, collecting own values **outer → inner**;","locale":"en"},"8045":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-91","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"prepend the *component-declared* metadata `locate(caller, name).fiber.inject[name]` (the value given in `inject: { name: meta }` of the declaring fiber) at the lowest priority. There is none for own provisions, and the walk stops at an isolation boundary;","locale":"en"},"8046":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-92","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"merge with `service[symbols.mergeIntercept]` (default `Object.assign({}, ...values)`, so right-biased).","locale":"en"},"8047":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-93","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"This is exactly `σ(k)(d(k) ⊕ ι(k))` from Definition 27, with ⊕ = shallow object merge (customizable per service). The `logger` service uses it for `{ name, level }` (`logger.ts:213-224`).","locale":"en"},"8048":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-94","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**Everything is in the root.** There is one `store`, one `props` and one `registry` per root; derived contexts differ only by their prototype-chained `isolate`/`intercept` tables and their `fiber`. This keeps \"is key k provided in realm r?\" a single map lookup.","locale":"en"},"8049":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-95","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**Provider identity** is the `Impl.uid`, a fresh counter value. This implements the \"name, not value\" discipline of the committed and target views.","locale":"en"},"8050":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-96","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**Isolation per realm symbol** implements the relaxed calculus \"disjoint within a realm\" (§4.4, see Metatheory).","locale":"en"},"8051":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-97","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**No compile-time checking**: declared vs. accessed keys are checked only at runtime, by the proxy (paper §5.1.4 notes this could be static).","locale":"en"},"8052":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"page","content":"Effects","bre