eading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"Tests documenting the semantics","locale":"en"},"8062":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/fiber.ts:60-363` and `utils.ts`. The paper counterpart is §3.1 and Algorithm 1; see Revertible effects.","locale":"en"},"8063":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"`fiber.ts:64-76`:","locale":"en"},"8064":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"An effect callback may therefore return:","locale":"en"},"8065":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Callback returns","locale":"en"},"8066":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Paper reading","locale":"en"},"8067":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"a function","locale":"en"},"8068":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"an effect function 𝔈Γ (the returned function is the inverse)","locale":"en"},"8069":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"`undefined`/`null`","locale":"en"},"8070":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"identity effect (nothing to undo)","locale":"en"},"8071":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"a `Promise<function>`","locale":"en"},"8072":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"async effect function","locale":"en"},"8073":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"a sync generator yielding disposers","locale":"en"},"8074":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"effect iterator ℑΓ, run to completion synchronously","locale":"en"},"8075":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"an async generator yielding disposers","locale":"en"},"8076":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"effect iterator with **iteration boundaries** that check a guard","locale":"en"},"8077":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Anything else throws `TypeError('Invalid effect')`.","locale":"en"},"8078":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`fiber.ts:240-290`. `EffectRunner { epoch, execute, collect, getOuterStack }` abstracts the two users of the engine, a single `ctx.effect` call and a fiber's whole `apply`:","locale":"en"},"8079":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`execute()` produces the effect value;","locale":"en"},"8080":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`collect(dispose)` records a yielded inverse;","locale":"en"},"8081":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`epoch` is the **guard**. For async iterators the loop runs `while (runner.epoch === oldEpoch)`; when the epoch changes, the loop stops after the current iteration lands and `iter.return()` is called so the generator's `finally` blocks run (`fiber.ts:269-285`).","locale":"en"},"8082":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"**Sync iterators are not interruptible** (there is no guard check); they could not be interrupted anyway in a single-threaded host. Every `collect` is type-checked (`safeCollect`).","locale":"en"},"8083":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`composeError(…, getOuterStack)` stitches the error stack together with the stack captured where the effect or plugin was *created* (`buildOuterStack`). This produces long stack traces that point at the user's `ctx.plugin(...)`/`ctx.effect(...)` call site. It is pure DX and JS-specific.","locale":"en"},"8084":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`fiber.ts:292-357`. `ctx.effect` is `ctx.fiber.effect` (mixed in by `ReflectService`). Step by step:","locale":"en"},"8085":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`assertActive()`: a fiber whose `uid` is `null` (removed) cannot create effects (`CordisError('INACTIVE_EFFECT')`).","locale":"en"},"8086":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"A local list `disposables` and a local `dispose()` that runs them **in reverse order**. If one returns a promise, the remaining ones are chained after it (sequential LIFO, `fiber.ts:298-311`).","locale":"en"},"8087":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`EffectMeta { label, children }` for introspection (`fiber.getEffects()`, used by tooling).","locale":"en"},"8088":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"A runner whose `epoch` is a boolean (`armed` in Algorithm 1) and whose `collect`:","locale":"en"},"8089":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"pushes the disposer into the local list,","locale":"en"},"8090":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"**removes it from the fiber's top-level list** (`this._disposables.delete(dispose)`), an ownership transfer (see below),","locale":"en"},"8091":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"records child metadata.","locale":"en"},"8092":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"Execute. On a synchronous throw, dispose what was collected and rethrow.","locale":"en"},"8093":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"Async failures: `task.catch(dispose)`. A failing async effect rolls back what it collected, and errors are logged rather than left unhandled.","locale":"en"},"8094":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"Build the returned **wrapper** (the disposer):","locale":"en"},"8095":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"at-most-once (`epoch` flips to `false`), Theorem 7's soundness invariant;","locale":"en"},"8096":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"flipping `epoch` also stops an in-flight async iterator at its next boundary;","locale":"en"},"8097":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"if setup is still running, disposal waits for it first (`task.then(dispose)`).","locale":"en"},"8098":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`wrapper.then(...)` makes the disposer **awaitable**: `await ctx.effect(...)` waits for setup to finish and resolves to a disposer.","locale":"en"},"8099":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`disposables.push(this._disposables.push(wrapper))`: the wrapper is registered in the **fiber's** list, and the function that removes it from that list is the first local disposable (so disposing an effect manually also unregisters it from the fiber).","locale":"en"},"8100":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#ownership","content":"Calling `ctx.effect` inside another effect's callback first registers the inner wrapper in the fiber's list. If the outer callback **yields or returns** that wrapper, `collect` moves ownership: the wrapper leaves the fiber's list and becomes part of the outer effect. If it is not yielded, it stays a direct child of the fiber. This implements the paper's \"parent composition\" (`ctx.dispose ← dispose ∘ ctx.dispose`) *without* nesting effect scopes: the accumulator of a fiber is the `DisposableList` `fiber._disposables`.","locale":"en"},"8101":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`utils.ts:5-40`. An insertion-ordered `Map<number, T>` plus a `WeakMap<T, number>`:","locale":"en"},"8102":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`push(v)` returns a remover `() => map.delete(sn)`;","locale":"en"},"8103":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`delete(v)` removes by identity;","locale":"en"},"8104":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`clear()` returns the values **reversed** (LIFO) and empties the list.","locale":"en"},"8105":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"It is used for fiber disposables, runtime fiber lists and per-fiber hook lists. It is an instance of the \"insert with fresh id, remove by id\" commutative-key design from paper §3.4.2 (see The context paradigm).","locale":"en"},"8106":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"The fiber's accumulator is not one composed closure but the list `fiber._disposables`. On unload (`fiber.ts:488-498`):","locale":"en"},"8107":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"Disposers are **initiated in reverse order but run concurrently**; each starts after a microtask. Inside a single effect they are sequential LIFO. The paper acknowledges this (\"`fiber.dispose` initiates a fiber's effects concurrently\", §5.1.3), and it is sound under the independence results (Theorem 43: inverses of independent effects can run in any order; see Metatheory).","locale":"en"},"8108":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"Ordered teardown *within* one logical effect must therefore be expressed by grouping it in one `ctx.effect` (a generator).","locale":"en"},"8109":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"Situation","locale":"en"},"8110":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"Behaviour","locale":"en"},"8111":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"sync throw in effect callback","locale":"en"},"8112":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"collected disposers run, error rethrown to caller","locale":"en"},"8113":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"async rejection in effect","locale":"en"},"8114":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"collected disposers run, error logged","locale":"en"},"8115":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"invalid yielded value","locale":"en"},"8116":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"`TypeError('Invalid effect')`","locale":"en"},"8117":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"error in a disposer during fiber unload","locale":"en"},"8118":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"logged; other disposers still run (`tests/fiber.spec.ts: 'dispose error'`, `service-dispose.spec.ts: 'releases dependencies after a cleanup error'`)","locale":"en"},"8119":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"effect on removed fiber","locale":"en"},"8120":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"`CordisError INACTIVE_EFFECT`","locale":"en"},"8121":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`tests/dispose.spec.ts` covers:","locale":"en"},"8122":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`dispose by plugin`, `dispose manually`, `yield dispose`;","locale":"en"},"8123":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async return 1/2`, `async yield 1`;","locale":"en"},"8124":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async yield 2/3 (aborted)`: disposing during setup stops the generator and disposes only what was yielded;","locale":"en"},"8125":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async yield (aborted, finally)`: `finally` runs;","locale":"en"},"8126":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async yield 4 (await dispose)`;","locale":"en"},"8127":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`return/yield with error`, `async yield invalid effect`.","locale":"en"},"8128":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"page","content":"Events and logger","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events","locale":"en"},"8129":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events","content":"Cordis's EventsService (registration as an effect, dispatch modes, internal events) and its logger (name resolution, levels, exporters).","locale":"en"},"8130":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#events","content":"`EventsService`","locale":"en"},"8131":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"Storage and registration","locale":"en"},"8132":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"Dispatch modes","locale":"en"},"8133":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"Internal events","locale":"en"},"8134":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"Logger","locale":"en"},"8135":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"Observations for a port","locale":"en"},"8136":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/events.ts` and `logger.ts`. In the paper, event listeners are the canonical *commutative key* (\"registration takes an entry of its own\", §3.4.2, see The context paradigm); the logger is an example of interception metadata.","locale":"en"},"8137":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#events","content":"`events.ts`. There is one instance on the root, mixed into contexts as `ctx.on/once/emit/parallel/serial/bail/waterfall`.","locale":"en"},"8138":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`_hooks: Record<name, Hook[]>` with `Hook { ctx, callback, prepend?, global?, removed? }`.","locale":"en"},"8139":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`on(name, listener, options)` (`events.ts:187-200`):","locale":"en"},"8140":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`assertActive()` on the calling fiber;","locale":"en"},"8141":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`listener = ctx.reflect.bind(listener)`: arguments and `this` are traced to the listener's context;","locale":"en"},"8142":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`bail('internal/listener', name, listener, options)` lets special events take over registration (used for the per-fiber `internal/update`);","locale":"en"},"8143":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"otherwise `register()`: a **`fiber.effect`** that pushes or unshifts the hook and returns `unregister` (which marks `removed = true`, splices, and deletes empty buckets). Because `this.ctx` is the traced use-site context, the effect is owned by the *listener's* fiber (see Services and traceability).","locale":"en"},"8144":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`once` disposes itself before calling the listener, so recursive emits and concurrent serial dispatches run it once.","locale":"en"},"8145":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`events.ts:110-163`:","locale":"en"},"8146":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"Mode","locale":"en"},"8147":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"Semantics","locale":"en"},"8148":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`emit`","locale":"en"},"8149":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"synchronous, all listeners, return ignored","locale":"en"},"8150":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`parallel`","locale":"en"},"8151":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`Promise.allSettled`; failures aggregated into `AggregateError`","locale":"en"},"8152":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`serial`","locale":"en"},"8153":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"sequential `await`; stops at the first \"bailed\" result (not `null/undefined/false`)","locale":"en"},"8154":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`bail`","locale":"en"},"8155":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"synchronous version of `serial`","locale":"en"},"8156":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`waterfall`","locale":"en"},"8157":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"middleware chain: each listener gets `(...args, next)`; `next()` may be called once (`next() called multiple times` otherwise); the last `next` calls the inner function","locale":"en"},"8158":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"Dispatch snapshots the listener list. Listeners removed during dispatch are skipped (`hook.removed`); listeners added during a waterfall run from the next dispatch.","locale":"en"},"8159":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"An optional first argument `thisArg` (an object) is the `this` for listeners. If it carries `[Context.filter]`, non-`global` hooks are filtered by `filter(hook.ctx)`. This is how realm-scoped events work: `internal/service` only reaches listeners in the same realm (`isolate.spec.ts: 'isolated event'`).","locale":"en"},"8160":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`internal/dispatch` is emitted for every non-internal dispatch when someone listens (tracing, devtools).","locale":"en"},"8161":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"`events.ts:211-224`:","locale":"en"},"8162":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"Event","locale":"en"},"8163":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"Emitted by","locale":"en"},"8164":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"8165":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"`internal/plugin(fiber)`","locale":"en"},"8166":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"fiber create / remove","locale":"en"},"8167":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"registry change","locale":"en"},"8168":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"`internal/replace(fiber)`","locale":"en"},"8169":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"`registry.replace`","locale":"en"},"8170":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/doc