erence-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"`internal/listener`","locale":"en"},"8190":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"`on()`","locale":"en"},"8191":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"intercept listener registration","locale":"en"},"8192":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"`internal/dispatch`","locale":"en"},"8193":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"every public dispatch","locale":"en"},"8194":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"observation","locale":"en"},"8195":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"The constructor installs:","locale":"en"},"8196":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"the `internal/listener` handler that turns `ctx.on('internal/update', …)` into a per-fiber hook list (`fiber._hooks['internal/update']`, itself a tracked effect);","locale":"en"},"8197":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"the global `internal/update` dispatcher that chains those hooks;","locale":"en"},"8198":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"the `internal/config` validator.","locale":"en"},"8199":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"`logger.ts`:","locale":"en"},"8200":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"`LoggerService` is a callable, `noShadow` service: `ctx.logger(name?)` returns a `Logger`; `ctx.logger.info(...)` is shorthand for `ctx.logger().info(...)`.","locale":"en"},"8201":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"**Name resolution:** explicit argument → interception metadata `{ name }` → the hyphenated name of the *caller's* fiber (`fiber.name` walks up to the first named runtime, else `root`). Inside a service method the caller is the service's def site, so log lines are attributed to the service (`logger.spec.ts` regression tests).","locale":"en"},"8202":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"**Level:** `exporter.levels[name] ?? exporter.levels.default ?? logger.level ?? INFO`; the levels are `ERROR=0, WARN=1, INFO=2, DEBUG=3`.","locale":"en"},"8203":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"**Messages:** `{ sn, ts, name, type, level, args, fiber?: WeakRef<Fiber> }`. Errors with a `cause` log the cause; non-empty `AggregateError`s are flattened.","locale":"en"},"8204":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-75","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"**Exporters** are registered with `logger.exporter(exp)` as a tracked effect, so a console exporter plugin unregisters on unload. A built-in exporter keeps a ring buffer of the last 1000 messages (for late-attached consoles).","locale":"en"},"8205":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-76","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"`Logger.format` implements printf-style `%s %d %i %f %o %O %c %C` with exporter-overridable formatters, colour codes (16/256-colour palettes hashed from the logger name) and per-line truncation (`maxLength`, default 10240).","locale":"en"},"8206":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-77","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"Events are just a service built on `ctx.effect`. Nothing in the lifecycle depends on them except the internal hooks (status, service, commit, update, config). A port can implement typed event channels and keep a small set of internal hook points.","locale":"en"},"8207":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-78","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"`waterfall` doubles as the extension mechanism for core behaviour (`internal/get`, `internal/config`, `internal/update`). In Rust these are better expressed as explicit hook traits or registries than as stringly-typed events.","locale":"en"},"8208":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-79","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"The logger maps naturally onto `tracing` (a span per fiber, the logger name as target), but the *exporter-as-effect* and buffer semantics must be kept if consoles attach at runtime.","locale":"en"},"8209":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-80","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"How kardia does this is described in API design.","locale":"en"},"8210":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"page","content":"Fiber lifecycle and registry","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","locale":"en"},"8211":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","content":"How Cordis core instantiates plugins as fibers, computes their targets, and drives them through the load/unload state machine with inertia and guards.","locale":"en"},"8212":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#plugins","content":"Plugins (components) and runtimes","locale":"en"},"8213":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#ctx-plugin","content":"`ctx.plugin(plugin, config)`","locale":"en"},"8214":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#replace","content":"`registry.replace(old, new)`","locale":"en"},"8215":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"The `Fiber` data structure","locale":"en"},"8216":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`FiberState` vs. the paper's θ","locale":"en"},"8217":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#instantiation","content":"Instantiation: O-Insert and O-Retire","locale":"en"},"8218":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#target","content":"Target computation: `_checkImpl` and `_refresh`","locale":"en"},"8219":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#state-machine","content":"The transition state machine","locale":"en"},"8220":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#set-epoch","content":"`_setEpoch(epoch)`: refresh","locale":"en"},"8221":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#reload","content":"`_reload()`: L-Begin … L-Finish / L-Divert","locale":"en"},"8222":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#unload","content":"`_unload()`: the guard and L-Unload","locale":"en"},"8223":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#update-state","content":"`_updateState(cb)`: state change and provider notification","locale":"en"},"8224":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#guards","content":"The two guards","locale":"en"},"8225":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"Waiting, updating, restarting","locale":"en"},"8226":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#failure","content":"Failure semantics","locale":"en"},"8227":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"Mapping to the nine rules","locale":"en"},"8228":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/fiber.ts` and `registry.ts`. The paper counterparts are §4.1–4.2 (the calculus, see Calculus) and §5.1.3 (Algorithms 4–5, see Implementation).","locale":"en"},"8229":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#plugins","content":"In `registry.ts`, a **plugin** (the paper's *component*) is one of:","locale":"en"},"8230":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#plugins","content":"`inject` is either `['a', 'b']` or `{ a: meta, b: meta }` (the values are component-declared interception metadata, Definition 26). `Inject.resolve` normalizes it to `Dict<meta | null>`; the `@Inject` decorator (on a class or a method) builds inherited inject tables (`registry.ts:17-61`).","locale":"en"},"8231":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#plugins","content":"`provide` is declarative only (used by the loader and tooling); the actual provision happens when the plugin calls `ctx.provide` or constructs a `Service`.","locale":"en"},"8232":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#plugins","content":"The *return value* of `apply` is treated as an effect (see Effects): a function, a promise, or a (async) generator of disposers.","locale":"en"},"8233":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#plugins","content":"`RegistryService` keeps a `Map<callback, Plugin.Runtime>`:","locale":"en"},"8234":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#plugins","content":"A runtime groups all fibers of one plugin; it is unregistered when its last fiber is removed (`fiber.ts:191-193`). `registry.counter` provides **fiber uids** (`++counter`, never reused).","locale":"en"},"8235":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#ctx-plugin","content":"`registry.ts:231-245`. It resolves aliases (see `replace`), calls `assertActive()` on the calling fiber, gets or creates the runtime, constructs `new Fiber(ctx, config, Inject.resolve(plugin.inject), runtime, outerStack)`, and returns an object whose prototype is the fiber and which is **thenable** (`await ctx.plugin(...)` ≡ `fiber.await()`). `ctx.inject(deps, cb)` is sugar for `ctx.plugin({ inject: deps, apply: cb })`.","locale":"en"},"8236":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#replace","content":"`registry.ts:185-209`. Swaps the implementation behind existing fibers **in place**:","locale":"en"},"8237":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#replace","content":"it records an alias `old → new`, so later `ctx.plugin(old)` instantiates `new` (aliases are followed in chains and can switch back);","locale":"en"},"8238":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#replace","content":"it moves every fiber of the old runtime to the new runtime via `fiber._replace(runtime, inject)`.","locale":"en"},"8239":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#replace","content":"`_replace` (`fiber.ts:401-416`) re-checks injections against the new `inject`, clears `_error`, bumps `_revision` and calls `_refresh()`. The fiber keeps its identity, parent and config but reloads with the new code. This is the primitive HMR uses (see HMR).","locale":"en"},"8240":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"`fiber.ts:115-220`:","locale":"en"},"8241":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"8242":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"Paper","locale":"en"},"8243":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"8244":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"`uid: number \\| null`","locale":"en"},"8245":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"name n","locale":"en"},"8246":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"`null` once removed (O-Remove)","locale":"en"},"8247":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"`parent: Context`","locale":"en"},"8248":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"π","locale":"en"},"8249":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"the context it was cr