hmr","content":"How @cordisjs/plugin-hmr replaces changed plugins in place as one transaction, with union-find commit units, and how it differs from the paper's Algorithm 10.","locale":"en"},"8372":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Integration","locale":"en"},"8373":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#module-graph","content":"Module graph","locale":"en"},"8374":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"`reconcile(callback)`: one transaction","locale":"en"},"8375":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"State preservation","locale":"en"},"8376":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"Watch mode","locale":"en"},"8377":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#error-ts","content":"`error.ts`","locale":"en"},"8378":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Paper vs. code","locale":"en"},"8379":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#node-specific","content":"What is Node-specific","locale":"en"},"8380":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/hmr/src/index.ts` and `error.ts`, plus `core/src/registry.ts:185-209` and `core/src/fiber.ts:401-416` (see `registry.replace`). The paper counterpart is §5.2.2, Algorithms 8–10; see Implementation.","locale":"en"},"8381":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","content":"**The implementation differs substantially from the paper's Algorithm 10** (see Paper vs. code).","locale":"en"},"8382":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`class Hmr extends Service`, service name `hmr`. Config:","locale":"en"},"8383":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"8384":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"8385":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"8386":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`base?`","locale":"en"},"8387":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`ctx.baseUrl`","locale":"en"},"8388":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"base directory","locale":"en"},"8389":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`watch.enabled`","locale":"en"},"8390":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`false`","locale":"en"},"8391":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"reload on file changes","locale":"en"},"8392":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`watch.files`","locale":"en"},"8393":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`['.', '!**/node_modules', '!**/.*']`","locale":"en"},"8394":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"glob filter","locale":"en"},"8395":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`watch.debounce`","locale":"en"},"8396":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"100 ms","locale":"en"},"8397":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"debounce before reloading","locale":"en"},"8398":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"It requires Node's internal ESM loader (`loader-utils` → `ModuleLoader.fromInternal()`, which needs `--expose-internals` or the `node-addon-require-builtin` addon); the constructor throws otherwise (fiber FAILED, no service).","locale":"en"},"8399":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Watching is an optional nested plugin `ctx.inject(['fs'], ...)`, active only while an `fs` service exists.","locale":"en"},"8400":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`[Service.init]` records the **host modules**: the import closure of `process.argv[1]` (the main program, core, loader…), which can only change by restarting the process.","locale":"en"},"8401":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"There is no loader-specific code: the loader imports plugins through the same internal ESM loader, so their modules are in the cache hmr inspects. hmr replaces plugins at the **registry** level, and loader entries keep their fibers.","locale":"en"},"8402":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#module-graph","content":"hmr keeps **no graph of its own**. It reads the live graph from Node's ESM `loadCache` (`ModuleJob.linked`) and the CJS `require.cache` each time (`_edges`, `closure`). Builtins (`node:`) are skipped; native addons (`.node`) cannot be reloaded.","locale":"en"},"8403":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"`index.ts:309-699`. Transactions are serialized on a promise queue; re-entrant calls from inside a transaction (from the callback, or from a plugin `apply` during stage 3) are rejected using `AsyncLocalStorage`.","locale":"en"},"8404":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Roots**: `await callback()` → absolute paths (validated).","locale":"en"},"8405":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Sweep**: evict *failed* ModuleJobs from the cache (Node keeps them and rethrows on every import), per type slot.","locale":"en"},"8406":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Match**: loaded modules whose path has a root as an ancestor (whole-segment match). Host modules and native addons → `skippedHostModules` (reported only).","locale":"en"},"8407":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Analyze**: reverse edges (excluding edges from host modules). `accepted` = the changed modules plus everything that transitively imports them; `declined` = host ∪ the rest. *(The paper's Algorithm 8 is a fixed point over forward imports with cycles defaulting to declined; the code is a simpler reverse-reachability worklist.)*","locale":"en"},"8408":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Discover**: for accepted modules, unwrap the exports and keep those that are registered plugins; **group them by runtime** (several modules can export the same plugin).","locale":"en"},"8409":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Stale plugins**: per runtime, the closure of its exporters through accepted modules. The module to re-import is the **outermost exporter** (which keeps the entry module's `inject`/`Config` metadata).","locale":"en"},"8410":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Backup and evict** every evicted URL (the whole multi-slot ESM entry + the CJS module).","locale":"en"},"8411":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Stage 1, import**, sequentially per stale plugin: re-import and check that the exports are a valid plugin (`registry.resolve`). *All fallible validation happens here, while only the module cache has been mutated*, so later stages need no rollback. No cache entry is restored before every plugin has been imported.","locale":"en"},"8412":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Partition into units** with union-find: two attempts join a unit if their **old ∪ new** closures share an evicted module (two plugins sharing a changed dependency must not end up with different instances of it).","locale":"en"},"8413":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Abort/commit**: units with any failed import are aborted and their modules restored. Orphaned evicted modules are restored with the aborted units they overlap (unless they reach a committed unit). Stage-1-loaded modules linked against restored modules are evicted.","locale":"en"},"8414":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Stage 2, replace (synchronous)**: `ctx.registry.replace(oldPlugin, newPlugin)` per committed attempt. `replace` aliases the old plugin key to the new one (later `ctx.plugin(old)` instantiates the new code) and calls `fiber._replace(newRuntime, newInject)` on each fiber: re-check injections, clear errors, bump the revision ⇒ **the same fiber object unloads and reloads in place** (identity, parent, config and loader entry preserved).","locale":"en"},"8415":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Stage 3, settle (concurrent)**: `await Promise.all(fibers.map(f => f.await().catch(noop)))`. There is **no rollback**: a plugin whose new `apply` throws stays FAILED (as on a cold start) and is retried on the next change.","locale":"en"},"8416":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"The result is `{ settledFibers, importFailures: { urls, error }[], skippedHostModules }`.","locale":"en"},"8417":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"Kept","locale":"en"},"8418":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"Lost","locale":"en"},"8419":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"fiber objects and uids, parents, configs, loader entries, services of *other* fibers","locale":"en"},"8420":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"all effects of the old instance (disposed by the normal unload path, which waits for dependents first, so the new instance never overlaps the old one) and the module-level state of re-imported modules","locale":"en"},"8421":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"Unrelated plugins are untouched. Different fibers reload concurrently (a slow drain does not delay a fast plugin).","locale":"en"},"8422":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"`index.ts:135-186`. `ctx.fs.watch(baseDir, { filter }).on('change', f => …)` → debounce → a serialized `flush` reconciling `retained ∪ stashed`.","locale":"en"},"8423":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"Host-module changes are warned about.","locale":"en"},"8424":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"Files of failed units are **retained** and retried together with the next change (a broken file and its dependency are retried together when only one of them is repaired).","locale":"en"},"8425":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"Only `change` events exist; a new file matters once a changed importer imports it.","locale":"en"},"8426":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#error-ts","content":"Pretty-prints esbuild `BuildFailure`s (tsx transpile errors) with `@babel/code-frame`.","locale":"en"},"8427":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Aspect","locale":"en"},"8428":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Paper (Algorithms 8–10)","locale":"en"},"8429":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Code","locale":"en"},"8430":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Classification","locale":"en"},"8431":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"forward fixed point; cycles default to declined","locale":"en"},"8432":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"reverse-reachability from changed modules; host modules declined","locale":"en"},"8433":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Stale detection","locale":"en"},"8434":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"per *entry* (`entry.url`)","locale":"en"},"8435":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"per *plugin runtime* (any registered plugin exported by an accepted module); loader-agnostic","locale":"en"},"8436":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Swap","locale":"en"},"8437":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"`entry.fiber.dispose(); entry.fiber ← ctx.use(import(url), config)`","locale":"en"},"8438":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"`registry.replace` → same fiber object reloads in place","locale":"en"},"8439":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Failure handling","locale":"en"},"8440":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"restore caches and rebuild *every* stale entry from backup, rethrow","locale":"en"},"8441":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"validation in stage 1; failing **units** (union-find) aborted and restored, others committed; failures of the new `apply` stay FAILED (no rollback)","locale":"en"},"8442":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Atomicity","locale":"en"},"8443":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"all-or-nothing","locale":"en"},"8444":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"per dependency-connected unit","locale":"en"},"8445":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Re-entrancy","locale":"en"},"8446":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-75","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"not discussed","locale":"en"},"8447":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-76","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"serialized queue + AsyncLocalStorage rejection","locale":"en"},"8448":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-77","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"The code's design is arguably stronger: commit/abort is per unit, and the \"point of no return\" is placed after the only fallible step that can be cleanly reverted.","locale":"en"},"8449":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-78","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#node-specific","content":"Everything in Module graph and steps 2, 7–8 and 10 of the transaction depend on Node's module caches and internals. The *algorithm* (match → accept → group by runtime → stage-1 validation → union-find units → replace in place → settle) is portable once a host-owned module registry exists. See Loader, include and HMR for kardia's design.","locale":"en"},"8450":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"page","content":"Include and group","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include","locale":"en"},"8451":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include","content":"How @cordisjs/plugin-include grafts a YAML/JSON file into the entry tree and keeps file and fibers in two-way sync, and what @cordisjs/plugin-group is.","locale":"en"},"8452":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#group","content":"Group","locale":"en"},"8453":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"Include: a file-backed `EntryTree`","locale":"en"},"8454":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"State","locale":"en"},"8455":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#io-loop","content":"The IO loop","locale":"en"},"8456":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"`_read()`","locale":"en"},"8457":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"`_write()`","locale":"en"},"8458":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#apply","content":"Tree application","locale":"en"},"8459":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"Journal","locale":"en"},"8460":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"Patches","locale":"en"},"8461":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#source-locations","content":"Source locations","locale":"en"},"8462":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"Errors","locale":"en"},"8463":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#design-notes","content":"Design notes","locale":"en"},"8464":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/include/src/{index,journal,patch}.ts` and `packages/group/src/index.ts`. The paper counterpart is §5.2.1 (\"`@cordisjs/include` loads an external configuration file (YAML or JSON) and grafts its entries in as a nested subtree\", see Implementation). The paper does not describe the synchronization machinery below; it is an implementation contribution.","locale":"en"},"8465":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#group","content":"`packages/group/src/index.ts` only re-exports `Group` from the loader (see `EntryTree` and `EntryGroup`). Its config is the list of child entries; config updates are absorbed in place as a keyed diff.","locale":"en"},"8466":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"`class Include extends EntryTree`, with `inject = ['loader']`, used as:","locale":"en"},"8467":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"It is a class plugin whose async-generator `[Service.init]` reads the file, yields `() => this.stop()`, and applies the tree. Its entries' composite ids are `<includeEntryId>:<localId>`; includes nest.","locale":"en"},"8468":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"`path` resolves against the parent tree's `baseUrl`; the include's own `ctx.baseUrl` becomes the file's directory (nested names and includes resolve relative to the file).","locale":"en"},"8469":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"`initial` is written if the file does not exist (ENOENT only); an unparsable existing file is **never overwritten**.","locale":"en"},"8470":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"`watch: true` → `ctx.inject(['fs'], ctx => ctx.fs.watch(filename).on('change', () => this.refresh()))`.","locale":"en"},"8471":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"An `internal/update` listener reconfigures in place (new `patches`) unless `path`/`watch` changed (then it does a full restart).","locale":"en"},"8472":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"8473":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"8474":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`filename`","locale":"en"},"8475":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"the resolved file","locale":"en"},"8476":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`type`","locale":"en"},"8477":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`application/json` or `application/yaml`, by extension","locale":"en"},"8478":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`cache?`","locale":"en"},"8479":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`{ content, data (parsed, ids assigned, unpatched), syntax? }`","locale":"en"},"8480":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`journal`","locale":"en"},"8481":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`Map<id, JournalRecord>`: tree-side changes not yet in the file","locale":"en"},"8482":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`index?`","locale":"en"},"8483":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`PatchIndex` (ownership)","locale":"en"},"8484":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`anonymous`","locale":"en"},"8485":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"ids invented for id-less file entries","locale":"en"},"8486":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`dirtyRead` / `dirtyWrite`","locale":"en"},"8487":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"IO flags","locale":"en"},"8488":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`_draining`","locale":"en"},"8489":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"the running IO loop","locale":"en"},"8490":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`_pendingTree` / `_applyTask`","locale":"en"},"8491":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"latest-wins application","locale":"en"},"8492":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#io-loop","content":"`index.ts:365-397`. A single-flight `_drain` runs `while (dirtyRead || dirtyWrite) { read-if-dirty; write-if-dirty }`. Read errors are **warnings** (half-written files are routine while editing) and stop the loop without writing (the file state is unknown); write errors are logged and the loop continues. `commit(change)` (from the tree) records into the journal, sets `dirtyWrite` and drains. `refresh()` (the watcher) sets `dirtyRead`.","locale":"en"},"8493":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Read; identical content ⇒ no-op (this also suppresses watcher feedback from its own writes).","locale":"en"},"8494":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Parse YAML (core schema regardless of `%YAML`, custom tag `!!js`, **errors and warnings both fatal**) or JSON; map issues to `file:line:col` (1-based, **UTF-16 columns**).","locale":"en"},"8495":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Validate the top-level array and the object entries; on failure keep the previous tree.","locale":"en"},"8496":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Assign ids to anonymous entries (stable across reads: the previous id is reused if the parent is the same and the options are deep-equal).","locale":"en"},"8497":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"If this is not the first read: a three-way **reconcile** of the journal against the old and new file states; the **file wins** on conflict, and each conflict is logged.","locale":"en"},"8498":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Cache and schedule an apply; if the journal is non-empty, schedule a write.","locale":"en"},"8499":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"Re-read; if the file changed externally, merge first.","locale":"en"},"8500":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"Snapshot-and-swap the journal; `routeJournal` sends each change to its **owner**: the file data, a patch in the include's own config, or an entry embedded in a patch.","locale":"en"},"8501":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"Patch changes are persisted by `this.ctx.fiber.update(newConfig)` (not awaited), which flows through `internal/commit` into the **parent** tree's file.","locale":"en"},"8502":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"File changes are dumped (**whole-file regeneration: comments and formatting are lost**) and written atomically: a temp file `.<base>.<pid>.<seq>.tmp` in the same directory, a stale-content check before **every** rename attempt, and rename with retries on EACCES/EPERM/EBUSY (11 attempts, linear backoff).","locale":"en"},"8503":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"Read-only files keep changes in memory, with a warning.","locale":"en"},"8504":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#apply","content":"`applyPatches(cache.data, patches)` (a fresh clone every time, so removing a patch reverts it) → `applyJournal(data, journal)` (overlay unwritten runtime changes) → latest-wins `root.update(tree)` → `EntryGroup` keyed reconciliation.","locale":"en"},"8505":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`journal.ts` contains pure functions:","locale":"en"},"8506":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"Function","locale":"en"},"8507":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"8508":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`record`","locale":"en"},"8509":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"deltas captured at report time","locale":"en"},"8510":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`mergeRecords`","locale":"en"},"8511":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"remove∘created-upsert = nothing; upsert after remove ⇒ `created:false`; changes merged newer-wins","locale":"en"},"8512":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`flatten`, `applyChanges`, `detach`, `place`, `applyJournal`","locale":"en"},"8513":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"apply records to entry lists","locale":"en"},"8514":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`reconcile(journal, base, theirs, fileOwned)`","locale":"en"},"8515":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"the three-way merge, where conflicting keys/moves/removals are dropped from the journal (\"file wins\")","locale":"en"},"8516":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"`patch.ts`:","locale":"en"},"8517":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"An **insert patch** `{ id?, insert: [...] }` appends entries into a group (or the root).","locale":"en"},"8518":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"An **override patch** `{ id, name?, ...keys }` overrides keys of an existing entry. `name`, if given, must match (a guard against patching a different plugin); overriding a group's `config` replaces its child list.","locale":"en"},"8519":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"`applyPatches` builds a `PatchIndex` recording the **owner** of every entry and key: `file`, `patch{index}` or `embedded{index, key}`. Later patches can address entries inserted by earlier ones.","locale":"en"},"8520":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"`routeJournal` writes each runtime edit back to its owner: patch-owned keys → the patch; entries inserted by a patch → inside the patch; the rest → the file.","locale":"en"},"8521":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#source-locations","content":"`_route(id, path)` finds where a value is written (file, patch, embedded) and delegates up through nested includes, producing virtual stack frames like `at a (inner.yml:1:3)` / `at inc (middle.yml:1:3)`. `walk` descends the YAML AST (resolving aliases to anchors); `seekExpr`/`scanScalar` map an offset inside an expression to a file offset (decoding quoted-scalar escapes).","locale":"en"},"8522":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"Error","locale":"en"},"8523":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"Side","locale":"en"},"8524":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"`ConfigFileError(stage: 'read'\\|'parse'\\|'validate', path, cause, issues[])`","locale":"en"},"8525":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"include","locale":"en"},"8526":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-75","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"`StaleWriteError`","locale":"en"},"8527":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-76","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"include (internal)","locale":"en"},"8528":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-77","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"`EntryValidationError`, `ModuleNotFoundError`, relocated `ValidationError`","locale":"en"},"8529":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-78","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"loader","locale":"en"},"8530":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-79","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#design-notes","content":"The include is the clearest example of the paper's *bidirectional* binding between configuration and fibers: runtime changes (plugin self-update or self-disable, API edits) flow back into files, file edits flow into fibers, and conflicts are resolved deterministically.","locale":"en"},"8531":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-80","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#design-notes","content":"Correctness relies on confluence (Theorem 80, see Metatheory): the include may apply intermediate trees, skip them (latest-wins) or apply them in a different order; the quiescent state depends only on the final tree.","locale":"en"},"8532":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-81","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#design-notes","content":"The synchronization core (journal, patch, reconcile, routing, id assignment) is **pure data transformation** over entry lists and is the most portable part of the code base.","locale":"en"},"8533":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"page","content":"Loader","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader","locale":"en"},"8534":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader","content":"How @cordisjs/plugin-loader turns a declarative tree of entries into fibers and keeps both in step: entries, expressions, reconciliation, managed realms and validation.","locale":"en"},"8535":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#role","content":"Role","locale":"en"},"8536":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#data-model","content":"Data model","locale":"en"},"8537":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-options","content":"`EntryOptions`","locale":"en"},"8538":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`Entry`","locale":"en"},"8539":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#two-fibers","content":"Two fibers per entry when `inject` is set","locale":"en"},"8540":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"Core hooks installed by the loader","locale":"en"},"8541":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#expressions","content":"Expressions","locale":"en"},"8542":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#algorithms","content":"Algorithms","locale":"en"},"8543":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-update","content":"`Entry.update(options, create, force)`","locale":"en"},"8544":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#init","content":"`init` / `_init`: concurrency-safe (re)initialization","locale":"en"},"8545":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-tree","content":"`EntryTree` and `EntryGroup`","locale":"en"},"8546":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#module-import","content":"Module import (Node-specific)","locale":"en"},"8547":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#managed-realms","content":"Managed realms","locale":"en"},"8548":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#validation","content":"Validation","locale":"en"},"8549":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#concurrency","content":"Concurrency model","locale":"en"},"8550":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/loader/src/**`. The paper counterparts are §5.2.1 *Declarative configuration* (see Implementation) and §4.4 *Configuration* (see Metatheory). File:line references on this page are relative to `packages/loader/src/`.","locale":"en"},"8551":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#role","content":"The loader turns a declarative **configuration tree** of *entries* into live fibers and keeps the two in step **bidirectionally**: config changes reconcile the fibers, and a plugin that updates its own config (`ctx.fiber.update`) or disposes itself (`ctx.fiber.dispose()`) is written back to its entry. It provides the `loader` service and owns the in-memory root tree; the same machinery is reused by `group` and `include` (see Include and group).","locale":"en"},"8552":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#role","content":"**Bootstrap** (`core/bin.js`): create a root `Context`, set `baseUrl` to the cwd, `await ctx.plugin(Loader)`, then `ctx.loader.create({ name: '@cordisjs/plugin-include', config: { path: './cordis.yml' } })`.","locale":"en"},"8553":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-options","content":"`config/entry.ts:8-16`, plus `isolate` from `config/isolate.ts:6-9`:","locale":"en"},"8554":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-options","content":"`null` means \"delete this key\" when merging; unknown keys are tolerated (only known keys are validated). `sortKeys` gives a stable order (`id`, `name`, the others alphabetically, `config` last) for file writes.","locale":"en"},"8555":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-options","content":"Mapping to Definition 81: `id` ✔, `url` → `name`, `isolate` ✔, `intercept` ✔, `config` ✔, `disabled` ✔, plus `inject` and `group`, which the paper does not list.","locale":"en"},"8556":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`config/entry.ts:55-68`:","locale":"en"},"8557":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-l