t of the root fiber's revertible effects: they must survive `root.fiber.dispose()`."],[7973,"It creates empty `isolate`/`intercept` tables (`Object.create(null)`)."],[7975,"It creates the **root fiber** `new Fiber(self, {}, {}, null, …)` (runtime `null` ⇒ root, uid 0, `ACTIVE`)."],[6656,"It gets the command's program, arguments, environment variables and working directory (`get_program`, `get_args`, `get_envs`, `get_current_dir`, or `to_std()` for a `std::process::Command`), and returns a `GuestProcess`: its stdin and stdout, optionally its stderr (`.stderr(…)`, for the exit report), and a `GuestChild`, the control the instance keeps until the process has ended (`id`, `kill`, `try_wait`, `wait`, as `std::process::Child` has them). `GuestProcess::from_child` takes a `std::process::Child` spawned with piped stdio. `StdSpawner`, the default, runs the command with `std::process` in the app's environment plus the command's variables. The instance kills its process when it is done with it, on dispose or when the guest fails."],[7976,"It instantiates the four built-in services on the root: `reflect`, `registry`, `events`, `logger`."],[8467,"It is a class plugin whose async-generator `[Service.init]` reads the file, yields `() => this.stop()`, and applies the tree. Its entries' composite ids are `<includeEntryId>:<localId>`; includes nest."],[7676,"It is a port of Kardia's core rather than a wrapper of the TypeScript Cordis:"],[8105,"It is used for fiber disposables, runtime fiber lists and per-fiber hook lists. It is an instance of the \"insert with fresh id, remove by id\" commutative-key design from paper §3.4.2 (see The context paradigm)."],[8238,"it moves every fiber of the old runtime to the new runtime via `fiber._replace(runtime, inject)`."],[5398,"It publishes every crate version that is not on crates.io yet, in dependency order (`cargo publish --workspace`; `xtask` is never published), then creates a GitHub release for the tag, with notes since the previous `release-*` tag."],[5408,"It publishes with **npm trusted publishing**: the publish job's `id-token: write` permission lets it mint a short-lived OIDC token that npm accepts for packages whose trusted publisher names this repository and workflow. No npm token is stored anywhere, and npm attaches a provenance statement to each version automatically (this needs the repository to stay public)."],[5403,"It publishes with the `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN` repository secret."],[8237,"it records an alias `old → new`, so later `ctx.plugin(old)` instantiates `new` (aliases are followed in chains and can switch back);"],[7926,"It renders a `[E]/[W]/[I]/[D]` prefix, a hashed-colour label, aligned continuation lines and an optional `+Nms` diff; `%o` uses `util.inspect`."],[8398,"It requires Node's internal ESM loader (`loader-utils` → `ModuleLoader.fromInternal()`, which needs `--expose-internals` or the `node-addon-require-builtin` addon); the constructor throws otherwise (fiber FAILED, no service)."],[7445,"It stays `Pending` until every declared service is available, then loads."],[7473,"It stops at a context that isolates the key again (an isolation boundary): the key is undeclared."],[7974,"It wraps itself in a `Proxy` with `ReflectService.handler`. This proxy *is* the context everybody sees; `this[symbols.root] = self`."],[6689,"Item"],[8694,"Iteration boundaries"],[6402,"Iteration boundaries and interruption"],[8725,"Iteration-boundary guard"],[4940,"Iteration-boundary staleness check"],[5160,"Iterator boundary"],[8005,"Its **inverse** is async:"],[6501,"its `apply` is running"],[6514,"its `FiberId` (never reused; `0` is the root)"],[6516,"its `FiberState`"],[7443,"its `inject` field (see Configuration)"],[7150,"its `TreeHandle`"],[6534,"its declaration, plugin definition, registry key, and plugin name (or its nearest named ancestor's)"],[6505,"its effects are being disposed"],[7057,"its group, and the group or tree its plugin owns"],[6507,"its last load failed; only `update` or a `registry.replace` recovers it (both clear the error)"],[7011,"its own root group and tree"],[6538,"its place in the tree, and whether it has been retired"],[7031,"its root group and context"],[7046,"its tree and context"],[6938,"Its unit is aborted: nothing in it is reloaded and the old module stays cached, so the running plugins keep their old code. Other units reload. In watch mode, its files are retried with the next batch."],[5815,"JavaScript stack frames;"],[1262,"JavaScript 栈帧；"],[8459,"Journal"],[5625,"JS `with(ctx) eval` cannot be ported. Decision point (Risks): adopt a side-effect-free expression language (recommended: CEL, or a small custom evaluator) whose identifiers resolve through `ctx.get_dyn(name)` and a serializable service view (`trait ExprValue { fn to_value(&self) -> Value }`), respecting the same evaluation-context table as the TS loader. Until then, `Expr` values are rejected with a clear validation issue."],[5584,"JS also implements `Fiber.setRecovery` and `Fiber.fail`, with supervision outside instance effects. Failure decisions follow cleanup and are cancelled on removal or policy changes. JS timers distinguish callback errors from instance failures and await in-flight callbacks during disposal. See the JS guide and cross-runtime acceptance."],[8947,"JS mechanism"],[5908,"JS recovery and cross-runtime isolation"],[1355,"JS 恢复与跨端隔离"],[4394,"JS 机制"],[1031,"JS 的 `Fiber.setRecovery` 与 `Fiber.fail` 也已实现，采用独立于实例效应的监督对象；清理完成后才处理失败，移除或切换策略会取消旧决定。JS timer 将回调异常与实例故障区分，清理时等待在途回调。见JS 使用指南及跨端验收。"],[1072,"JS 的 `with(ctx) eval` 无法移植。待定决策（风险）：采用一种无副作用的表达式语言（推荐 CEL，或一个小型自定义求值器），其标识符通过 `ctx.get_dyn(name)` 和可序列化的服务视图（`trait ExprValue { fn to_value(&self) -> Value }`）解析，并遵循与 TS 加载器相同的求值上下文表。在此之前，`Expr` 值会被拒绝，并给出明确的校验问题。"],[2615,"JSON 文件也会被当作 YAML 解析一遍（JSON 即 YAML），因此得到同样的位置；"],[2738,"JSON 配置"],[3193,"kardia"],[7746,"kardia"],[7655,"kardia composes a Rust app. When part of the app is TypeScript, as in a Tauri app whose interface runs in a webview, the `@kardiajs` packages give that side the same model: plugins, services, revertible effects and lifecycle. The **bridge** connects the two runtimes."],[5173,"kardia implements the model of the paper *A Programming Paradigm for Spatiotemporal Composability* (arXiv:2608.25512; 92 pages; Shi, Zhang and Cui; Peking University and DeepSeek-AI). This section summarises the paper's theory: its problem statement, contributions and vocabulary, then one page per part of the paper. Definition, theorem, lemma and algorithm numbers are always the paper's."],[7756,"kardia is a Rust implementation of Cordis, the plugin framework built on *spatiotemporal composability* (paper)."],[8973,"kardia is a Rust port of Cordis, the TypeScript plugin framework described in the paper A Programming Paradigm for Spatiotemporal Composability. The Concepts section covers the paper's model; this section covers the **code**: how the TypeScript implementation actually realizes that model, where it refines or departs from the paper, and which parts a port must preserve."],[5311,"kardia is developed at github.com/licyk/kardia. This page covers the Rust workspace, the npm packages under `js/`, their CI and releases, and this documentation site."],[7841,"kardia is split into ten crates, all published on crates.io. Most projects depend only on `kardia`; a guest plugin depends only on `kardia-guest`."],[3165,"kardia 上的 Rust 插件"],[3288,"kardia 分为十个 crate，全部发布在 crates.io 上。大多数项目只需依赖 `kardia`；访客插件只需依赖 `kardia-guest`。"],[758,"kardia 在 github.com/licyk/kardia 上开发。本页介绍 Rust 工作区、`js/` 下的 npm 包、它们的 CI 与发布，以及本文档站点。"],[1349,"kardia 如何测试：移植的 TypeScript spec 套件及其运行时、针对论文元理论的基于模型的属性测试、单元测试和工具。"],[3230,"kardia 如何用 Rust 重建它"],[728,"kardia 如何用每个根一把锁、返回动作的临界区以及派生的转换任务，重现 JavaScript 的运行至完成原子性。"],[4276,"kardia 如何落实这些，见生命周期、API 设计、加载器、include 与 HMR，以及列出全部偏离的状态。"],[620,"kardia 实现的是论文 *A Programming Paradigm for Spatiotemporal Composability*（arXiv:2608.25512；92 页；Shi、Zhang、Cui；北京大学与 DeepSeek-AI）中的模型。本部分概述论文的理论：先介绍其问题陈述、贡献和术语，然后论文的每一部分各占一页